1
00:00:08,914 --> 00:00:14,200
The Life of Muhammadﷺ, The Madina period, volume 1

2
00:00:14,377 --> 00:00:16,508
by Imam Anwar Al_Awlaki

3
00:00:17,793 --> 00:00:23,965
اَلْحَمْدُ لله رَبِّ الْعَالَمِيْنْ ، وَالصَّلَاةُ وَالسَّلَامُ عَلى سَيِّدِنَا محمد وَعَلَى اَلِهِ وَصَحْبِهِ وَسَلِّمْ تَسْلِيْمًا كَثِيْراَّ

4
00:00:24,451 --> 00:00:27,133
أما بعد، السلام عليكم ورحمة الله وبركاته

5
00:00:28,762 --> 00:00:35,985
What was the first project that Rasool Allah ﷺ started when he reached to Madina.?

6
00:00:36,978 --> 00:00:41,192
If we take the four projects, the first four projects

7
00:00:41,887 --> 00:00:46,364
that Rasool Allah ﷺ started with in Madina, these four projects are;

8
00:00:46,476 --> 00:00:48,087
Number one, The Masjid(مسجد).

9
00:00:48,997 --> 00:00:51,947
Number two, establishing brotherhood.

10
00:00:52,544 --> 00:00:58,624
Number three, a covenant that would govern the relationships between the different people of Madina.

11
00:00:58,898 --> 00:01:01,827
And number four, the establishment of the army.

12
00:01:03,027 --> 00:01:05,336
We start with the first project and that is the Masjid(مسجد).

13
00:01:06,377 --> 00:01:11,035
The Masijd(مسجد) was the first thing Rasool Allah ﷺ did, when he arrived to Madina.

14
00:01:11,987 --> 00:01:15,306
And you can notice that it was the first thing, he did when he arrived at Qubaa(قباء),

15
00:01:15,725 --> 00:01:18,948
the first thing he did when he arrived to Qubaa(قباء), was to build the Masjid(مسجد) of Qubaa(قباء).

16
00:01:19,255 --> 00:01:23,406
And the first thing, he does inside Madina is to build Al-Masjid-e-Nabawi(ألمسجد النبوي).

17
00:01:24,738 --> 00:01:29,538
This is because Al-Masjid(المسجد), is the center of learning for the Muslims,

18
00:01:29,735 --> 00:01:35,606
and that's why it was the first project that Rasool Allah ﷺ started with in Madina.

19
00:01:35,864 --> 00:01:39,966
Rasool Allah ﷺ had Dar-Ul-Arqam(دارالارقم) in Makkah, and now he's building the Masjid(مسجد),

20
00:01:40,482 --> 00:01:43,066
which expands the role of Dar-Ul-Arqam(دارالارقم).

21
00:01:43,649 --> 00:01:49,272
Dar-Ul-Arqam(دارالارقم) was a secret location, where the Muslims would meet and pray and teach.

22
00:01:49,668 --> 00:01:53,247
But now since Rasool Allah ﷺ has established an Islamic State,

23
00:01:53,664 --> 00:01:55,688
it wasn't in a secret location, anymore.

24
00:01:55,871 --> 00:01:59,654
It was public, it was the Masjid(مسجد), Al-Masjid-e-Nabawi(ألمسجد النبوي).

25
00:02:00,614 --> 00:02:02,432
How did he choose the location?

26
00:02:03,159 --> 00:02:08,280
Rasool Allah ﷺ was riding his camel and people were pulling it,

27
00:02:08,563 --> 00:02:11,015
everyone wants to pull it towards their direction.

28
00:02:11,289 --> 00:02:14,857
Rasool Allah ﷺ said; Leave it, because it has been commanded by Allah.

29
00:02:16,001 --> 00:02:24,626
So, the camel was going through the streets of Madina and then it stopped in this particular location,

30
00:02:25,598 --> 00:02:28,669
which was a field for drying dates,

31
00:02:29,189 --> 00:02:34,278
when dates become ripe, they need to be dried and they would do that in an open place,

32
00:02:34,406 --> 00:02:40,577
so that it would be exposed to the sun and the water inside the dates would evaporate.

33
00:02:41,328 --> 00:02:44,226
And this field belonged to two orphans in Madina.

34
00:02:44,996 --> 00:02:47,932
So, Rasool Allah ﷺ when the camel chose this location,

35
00:02:48,609 --> 00:02:51,030
Rasool Allah ﷺ said: This is our place.

36
00:02:51,289 --> 00:02:52,319
هَذَالْمَنْزِلْ

37
00:02:52,479 --> 00:02:54,328
This is the location of the Masjid(مسجد).

38
00:02:54,549 --> 00:02:57,776
And this is the location of his living quarters.

39
00:02:59,149 --> 00:03:03,081
Rasool Allah wanted to buy this area from the two orphans.

40
00:03:03,121 --> 00:03:06,415
They said: No, we're going to give it to you, O Rasool Allah, we're going to give it to you.

41
00:03:06,987 --> 00:03:10,347
There were some graves in there, graves of Mushrikeen(مشركين),

42
00:03:10,387 --> 00:03:14,045
Rasool Allah ﷺ uncovered those graves and changed the location.

43
00:03:15,016 --> 00:03:17,273
And they started building Al-Masjid-e-Nabawi(ألمسجد النبوي),

44
00:03:18,259 --> 00:03:20,021
they built it from mud bricks

45
00:03:20,843 --> 00:03:23,971
and the roof was palm leaves.

46
00:03:24,210 --> 00:03:28,482
So, when it would rain, it would drop right, on top of their heads,

47
00:03:28,989 --> 00:03:33,512
very simple, the floor was sand.

48
00:03:34,316 --> 00:03:41,189
Even though it was very simple, it was the most blessed Masjid(مسجد), that's where the first generation graduated from.

49
00:03:42,429 --> 00:03:46,267
Rasool Allah ﷺ joined the Sahabah in the building of the Masjid(مسجد),

50
00:03:46,292 --> 00:03:50,674
he was giving them an example of himself joining and working.

51
00:03:51,094 --> 00:03:52,983
So, the poet among them said;

52
00:03:53,761 --> 00:03:58,059
لَئِنْ قَعَدْنَا وَالنَّبِيُّ يَعْمَلْ ذَلِكَ مِنَّا اَلْعَمَلٌ مُدَلَّلْ

53
00:03:58,319 --> 00:04:01,615
If we sit down, while the Messenger of Allah is working

54
00:04:01,913 --> 00:04:05,207
that is a misguided act on our behalf.

55
00:04:06,029 --> 00:04:13,728
So, Rasool Allah ﷺ himself was carrying the bricks and building the Masjid(مسجد) with the Sahabahرضي الله عنهم.

56
00:04:16,030 --> 00:04:19,168
Some lessons from the building of the Masjid(مسجد).

57
00:04:19,208 --> 00:04:19,956
Number one,

58
00:04:21,208 --> 00:04:23,683
the Masjid(مسجد) is the first thing that Rasool Allah ﷺ did.

59
00:04:23,780 --> 00:04:24,763
Allahعَزّوجَلّ says;

60
00:04:24,827 --> 00:04:27,553
الَّذِينَ إِنْ مَكَّنَّاهُمْ فِي الْأَرْضِ أَقَامُوا الصَّلَاةَ

61
00:04:28,339 --> 00:04:33,235
The ones, whom when we establish in land, they would establish prayers,

62
00:04:34,098 --> 00:04:37,036
when we give them authority in land they would establish Salah(صلاة).

63
00:04:37,262 --> 00:04:41,373
So, Allah has given Rasool Allah ﷺ and the Sahabah authority in the land.

64
00:04:41,739 --> 00:04:44,005
The first thing they did is to establish Salah(صلاة),

65
00:04:44,346 --> 00:04:47,804
and by establishing the Masjid(مسجد), they're establishing the center of Salah(صلاة).

66
00:04:48,369 --> 00:04:49,795
What is the role of the Masjid(مسجد).?

67
00:04:51,068 --> 00:04:52,804
Allahعَزّوجَلّ says in Qur'an;

68
00:04:53,079 --> 00:04:59,434
فِي بُيُوتٍ أَذِنَ اللَّهُ أَنْ تُرْفَعَ وَيُذْكَرَ فِيهَا اسْمُهُ

69
00:04:59,720 --> 00:05:05,698
يُسَبِّحُ لَهُ فِيهَا بِالْغُدُوِّ وَالْآصَالِ۝

70
00:05:06,139 --> 00:05:14,649
رِجَالٌ لَا تُلْهِيهِمْ تِجَارَةٌ وَلَا بَيْعٌ عَنْ ذِكْرِ اللَّهِ

71
00:05:15,192 --> 00:05:27,559
لَا تُلْهِيهِمْ تِجَارَةٌ وَلَا بَيْعٌ عَنْ ذِكْرِ اللَّهِ وَإِقَامِ الصَّلَاةِ وَإِيتَاءِ الزَّكَاةِۙ

72
00:05:28,027 --> 00:05:36,090
 يَخَافُونَ يَوْمًا تَتَقَلَّبُ فِيهِ الْقُلُوبُ وَالْأَبْصَارُ۝

73
00:05:36,479 --> 00:05:43,551
ليَجْزِيَهُمُ اللَّهُ أَحْسَنَ مَا عَمِلُوا وَيَزِيدَهُمْ مِنْ فَضْلِهِ ۗ

74
00:05:43,957 --> 00:05:52,638
وَاللَّهُ يَرْزُقُ مَنْ يَشَاءُ بِغَيْرِ حِسَابٍ۝

75
00:05:53,229 --> 00:05:56,304
"In houses which Allah has ordered to be raised

76
00:05:56,891 --> 00:05:59,319
and that His name be mentioned there in,

77
00:05:59,651 --> 00:06:04,010
exalting Him within them in the morning and evening are men,

78
00:06:04,511 --> 00:06:11,265
whom neither commerce nor sale distracts them from performance of prayer and giving Zakah(زكواة)

79
00:06:11,931 --> 00:06:15,576
They fear a Day in which the hearts and eyes will turn about

80
00:06:16,005 --> 00:06:20,852
that Allah may reward them the best of what they did, and increase them from His bounty.

81
00:06:21,277 --> 00:06:25,148
And Allah gives provision to whom He wills, without account."

82
00:06:25,581 --> 00:06:27,187
So, the Masjid(مسجد) is just a building.

83
00:06:28,102 --> 00:06:30,659
But the real essence of the Masjid(مسجد) are the people inside the Masjid(مسجد).

84
00:06:31,143 --> 00:06:32,564
That is the spirit of the Masjid(مسجد).

85
00:06:33,045 --> 00:06:35,996
So, Allahعَزّوجَلّ says; the house of Allah in them are men,

86
00:06:36,648 --> 00:06:41,345
who are not distracted by commerce, they're not distracted by money, they're not distracted by making a living.

87
00:06:41,912 --> 00:06:43,413
They worship Allahعَزّوجَلّ.

88
00:06:43,779 --> 00:06:46,310
They do make a living, they do work, they do business,

89
00:06:46,540 --> 00:06:49,675
but when they are in the Masjid(مسجد), they are remembering Allahعَزّوجَلّ.

90
00:06:49,969 --> 00:06:51,985
Duniya(دنيا) is not on their mind.

91
00:06:52,809 --> 00:06:56,128
So, the Masjid(مسجد) is a place of prayer and remembrance of Allah.

92
00:06:56,191 --> 00:06:59,937
That's the first and most important role of the Masjid(مسجد),

93
00:07:00,064 --> 00:07:02,945
it's a place of Zikr(ذكر) and a place of Salah(صلاة).

94
00:07:03,328 --> 00:07:03,974
Number two,

95
00:07:04,077 --> 00:07:05,807
the Masjid(مسجد) is the center of learning,

96
00:07:06,244 --> 00:07:09,474
Dar-Ul-Arqam(دارالارقم) in Makkah and Masjid Al-Nabwi(مسجدالنبوي) in Madina

97
00:07:09,761 --> 00:07:13,710
That is where Rasool Allah ﷺ would give his Khutba(خطبه) that's where he would give his talks,

98
00:07:13,735 --> 00:07:19,397
that's where the Sahabah(صحابه) would come together in circles and studying the book of Allah.

99
00:07:20,447 --> 00:07:24,371
Rasool Allah ﷺ says in the Hadith(حديث), if people come together in the house of Allah,

100
00:07:24,466 --> 00:07:28,390
studying the book of Allahعَزّوجَلّ and reading it, Allah will give them four things,

101
00:07:28,823 --> 00:07:30,925
1. Sakeena(سكينه), tranquility,

102
00:07:31,496 --> 00:07:32,917
2.  Mercy(رحمه),

103
00:07:33,425 --> 00:07:36,869
and number three, angels would surround them

104
00:07:37,082 --> 00:07:41,326
and Number four, Allah will mention their names in a gathering better than theirs.

105
00:07:43,060 --> 00:07:48,415
Number three, the Masjid(مسجد) is a place for Muslims to meet, so it plays a social role.

106
00:07:49,445 --> 00:07:52,784
And Muslims who pray Jam'maa(جماعة) would meet five times a day,

107
00:07:53,300 --> 00:07:55,649
that strengthens the bonds of brotherhood.

108
00:07:56,923 --> 00:07:58,426
They also meet on Jum'ah(جمعه)

109
00:07:58,870 --> 00:08:03,610
and the word Jum'ah(جمعه) and Jama'a(جماعه), it mean congregation, people coming together, it's a gathering.

110
00:08:04,729 --> 00:08:08,173
Number four, the Masjid(مسجد) was a dwelling for the traveler, and the poor,

111
00:08:08,213 --> 00:08:09,846
and we're going to talk about Ahl-Us-Suffah(أهل الصفه),

112
00:08:10,143 --> 00:08:12,953
and the special place that was built for them, in the Masjid(مسجد).

113
00:08:14,183 --> 00:08:17,928
Number five, the Masjid(مسجد) was a place where the armies would be sent out from.

114
00:08:18,429 --> 00:08:20,573
That is where the Luw'aa(لؤوا) would be set,

115
00:08:20,748 --> 00:08:25,272
the banners or the standards of war, would be handed out inside the Masjid(مسجد).

116
00:08:26,339 --> 00:08:29,540
And finally, Masjid(مسجد) is place for Da'wah(دعوة),

117
00:08:30,235 --> 00:08:35,111
when the Christians from Najraan(نجران) in Yemen came to visit Rasool Allah ﷺ where did they stay?

118
00:08:35,600 --> 00:08:36,678
They didn't stay in hotels.

119
00:08:36,798 --> 00:08:42,610
They weren't refused, they weren't banned from entering the Masjid(مسجد), they lived in the Masjid(مسجد).

120
00:08:42,829 --> 00:08:45,453
They lived in the Masjid(مسجد), so that they can see the Muslims pray.

121
00:08:45,729 --> 00:08:50,008
They could hold their discussions and conversations with Rasool Allah ﷺ.

122
00:08:50,278 --> 00:08:53,542
So, the Masjid(مسجد) plays an important role, in Da'wah(دعوة).

123
00:08:53,876 --> 00:08:58,415
We said that the Masjid(مسجد) of Rasool Allah ﷺ, Al-Masjid-e-Nabawi(المسجدالنبوي) was simple.

124
00:08:58,622 --> 00:09:01,713
It didn't have all of those fancy decorations.

125
00:09:01,898 --> 00:09:05,223
So, what's the ruling on those decorations to start with.?

126
00:09:06,391 --> 00:09:12,474
The scholars say that Tash'heed(تشهيد) is allowed, while Zakhrafah(زخرفه) and Naqsh(نقش) is not.

127
00:09:13,421 --> 00:09:19,369
Tash'heed(تشهيد), means having good building material, good building for the Masjid(مسجد) itself.

128
00:09:20,061 --> 00:09:22,376
So, the Masjid(مسجد) of Rasool Allah was made out of mud bricks,

129
00:09:22,435 --> 00:09:28,003
but later on, they built it from stone, they had some pillars in there, that is allowed

130
00:09:28,501 --> 00:09:32,016
That was allowed, having a roof made out of wood.

131
00:09:33,069 --> 00:09:35,711
In one of the expenses of Al-Masjid-e-Nabwi(ألمسجد النبوي) that was allowed,

132
00:09:35,758 --> 00:09:39,049
because these things happened during the time of Al-Khulafah-Ar-Rashidoon(خلفاءالراشدون).

133
00:09:39,616 --> 00:09:44,767
But the decoration of the Masjid(مسجد), the scholars have a difference of opinion,

134
00:09:44,847 --> 00:09:47,707
some of them say it is Haram(حرام) and some say it's Makrooh(مكروه).

135
00:09:48,942 --> 00:09:51,741
Now even the ones who say that it is Makrooh(مكروه),

136
00:09:51,781 --> 00:09:57,812
they say that if somebody designates money to be used as a Waqf(وقف), as a trust for a Masjid(مسجد),

137
00:09:58,154 --> 00:10:02,952
it is Haram(حرام) to use that money to decorate the Masjid(مسجد), it needs to go into the building of the Masjid(مسجد).

138
00:10:03,754 --> 00:10:06,160
So, Abu Darda(ابودرداء) for example, he says;

139
00:10:06,438 --> 00:10:14,075
اِذَ زَخْرَفْتُمْ مَسَاجِدَكُمْ، وَزَوَّقْتُمْ مَصَاحِفَكُمْ فَالَدمَارُعَلَيْكُمْ

140
00:10:15,131 --> 00:10:22,517
If you decorate your Qur'an, the Mus'haf(مصحف) and you decorate your Masjid(مسجد), then you would perish,

141
00:10:23,211 --> 00:10:27,938
because that's the sign of preferring symbols over substance.

142
00:10:29,841 --> 00:10:33,482
The Masjid-e-Nabwi(ألمسجد النبوي) was simple, mud bricks.

143
00:10:34,051 --> 00:10:38,012
But the best men of this Ummah(امة) graduated from Al-Masjid-e-Nabwi(ألمسجدالنبوي).

144
00:10:38,355 --> 00:10:42,024
And now we have huge buildings, magnificent.

145
00:10:42,646 --> 00:10:43,980
But what are the results,

146
00:10:45,091 --> 00:10:53,345
they merely show the sophisticated architecture and all the money that was thrown into, those huge buildings, that's about it.

147
00:10:55,056 --> 00:10:57,566
Another lesson Tarbiyah(تربيعة) through practice,

148
00:10:58,241 --> 00:11:00,808
Rasool Allah ﷺ was teaching the Sahabah(صحابه) by practicing.

149
00:11:01,731 --> 00:11:03,577
He was building the Masjid(مسجد) with them.

150
00:11:03,760 --> 00:11:06,355
He wasn't just giving them instructions from a high place.

151
00:11:06,922 --> 00:11:11,383
He was joining them in the field and showing them, what it means to be a Muslim.

152
00:11:12,812 --> 00:11:17,794
The next lesson, specialization is respected in Islam.

153
00:11:18,398 --> 00:11:22,263
And people should be told to do what they're capable of doing and what they're best at.

154
00:11:22,886 --> 00:11:25,508
This is an important thing for the Muslim leader to learn.

155
00:11:25,932 --> 00:11:28,305
Because when they were building the Masjid-Al-Nabwi(مسجد النبوي),

156
00:11:28,841 --> 00:11:31,273
there was a man from Najd(نجد) who was with them.

157
00:11:32,086 --> 00:11:34,804
And this man was a builder, he himself.

158
00:11:35,491 --> 00:11:39,502
So, he asked Rasool Allah ﷺ, should I join you in carrying the bricks?

159
00:11:39,716 --> 00:11:42,786
Rasool Allah ﷺ said, No, do not carry the bricks with us.

160
00:11:42,986 --> 00:11:46,122
You make the mixture for the bricks and make them

161
00:11:46,919 --> 00:11:49,629
and because other people can carry the bricks,

162
00:11:50,161 --> 00:11:52,546
but you need to focus on what you are best at.

163
00:11:52,684 --> 00:11:55,551
And that is making these bricks for us.

164
00:11:56,178 --> 00:12:05,123
So, if this man was carrying bricks, you would have people who are not as expert as he was, mixing the bricks.

165
00:12:05,621 --> 00:12:13,405
So, Rasool Allah ﷺ would devote him to this act and have other people carry the bricks.

166
00:12:13,994 --> 00:12:19,051
So in our Islamic work, not everybody has to do the same thing.

167
00:12:19,891 --> 00:12:22,586
Not everyone needs to be a good Daiyah(داعيه).

168
00:12:22,769 --> 00:12:25,102
Not everyone needs to become a scholar.

169
00:12:25,364 --> 00:12:27,475
Not everyone needs to be an Imaam(إمام).

170
00:12:27,991 --> 00:12:32,598
Let people do what they're capable of doing because Allah gives different people different gifts.

171
00:12:34,111 --> 00:12:40,590
And the good leader is the one, who recognizes the abilities of his followers and advises them,

172
00:12:41,151 --> 00:12:45,764
and how to strengthen the gifts that Allahسبحانه و تعالى has given them

173
00:12:45,789 --> 00:12:52,619
and how to take advantage of those abilities for the sake of the benefit of Islam and Muslims.

174
00:12:54,621 --> 00:12:57,345
Some virtues of Al-Masjid-Al-Nabwi(مسجد النبوي)

175
00:12:59,048 --> 00:13:01,157
Rasool Allah ﷺ says;

176
00:13:01,228 --> 00:13:08,922
صَلَاةٌ فِيْ مَسْجِدِيْ هَذَ اَفْضَلْ مِنْ اَلْفِ صَلَاتٍ فِيْمَا سِوَاه اِلَّا مَسْجِدِالْحَرَامْ

177
00:13:10,384 --> 00:13:13,011
Rasool Allah ﷺ says in the Hadith(حديث) narrated by Al-Bukhari(البخاريْ)

178
00:13:13,436 --> 00:13:21,929
one Salah(صلاة) in my Masjid(مسجد) it is better than 1000 Salah(صلاة) in any other Masjid except Masjid Al-Haraam(مسجدالحرام), Al-Ka'aba(اَلْكَعْبَه).

179
00:13:23,526 --> 00:13:28,932
Which means that if you pray one Ishaa(عشاء) for example, in Al-Masjid-Al-Nabwi(مسجد النبوي),

180
00:13:28,996 --> 00:13:36,318
it counts as if you have prayed Ishaa(عشاء) for 83 years in any other Masjid(مسجد),

181
00:13:36,697 --> 00:13:44,106
so if you're praying Ishaa(عشاء) every evening in another Masjid(مسجد) for 83 years,

182
00:13:44,655 --> 00:13:47,830
that counts as one Ishaa(عشاء) in Al-Masjid-Al-Nabwi(مسجد النبوي),

183
00:13:47,870 --> 00:13:51,408
that's how much blessing there is, in praying in Al-Masjid-Al-Nabwi(مسجد النبوي).

184
00:13:52,020 --> 00:13:53,312
Rasool Allah ﷺ also says;

185
00:13:53,392 --> 00:14:02,178
لَا تُشَدُّ الرِحَالُ اِلَّا اِلَى ثَلَاثَةِ مَسْاجِدْ، مَسْجِدِ الْحَرَامْ، وَمَسْجِدِ الْاَقْصَى، وَمَسْجِدِيْ هَذَا

186
00:14:03,197 --> 00:14:09,255
You should not travel to visit a Masjid(مسجد), except if it is one of three Masjid(مسجد)s

187
00:14:09,865 --> 00:14:14,915
Al-Masjid Al-Haraam(مسجدالحرام), Al-Ka'aba(ألكعبه), Al-Masjid Al-Aksaa(مسجد الاقصى) in Jerusalem

188
00:14:15,173 --> 00:14:18,957
and this Masjid(مسجد) of mine, Al-Masjid-Al-Nabwi(مسجد النبوي).

189
00:14:19,707 --> 00:14:20,943
And Rasool Allah ﷺ says:

190
00:14:20,983 --> 00:14:26,841
مَا بَيْنَ بَيْتِيْ وَمِمْبَرِي ْرَوْضَةٌ مِنْ الرِّيَاضِ الْجَنَّة، وَمِمْبَرِيْ عَلَى حَوْضِي

191
00:14:27,590 --> 00:14:31,073
Rasool Allah ﷺ says, between my house and my pulpit

192
00:14:32,604 --> 00:14:40,936
is a garden from among the gardens of Paradise and my pulpit is on my pool, Al-Kauser(ألكوثر),

193
00:14:41,067 --> 00:14:46,562
the pool that Rasool Allah ﷺ would be given on the Day of Judgment and this is in Al-Bukhari(بخاريْ).

194
00:14:48,411 --> 00:14:54,700
Abdullah Bin Zaid(عبدالله بن زيد), one of the Sahabah(صحابه) of Rasool Allah ﷺ saw a dream,

195
00:14:55,907 --> 00:15:03,020
at that time Rasool Allah ﷺ has finished constructing the Masjid Al-Nabawi(مسجد النبوي)

196
00:15:03,627 --> 00:15:09,310
and now they were thinking about ways to invite people to the prayer.

197
00:15:10,047 --> 00:15:16,363
So, some suggestions were using a bell, similar to what the Christians do.

198
00:15:16,929 --> 00:15:19,233
Another suggestion was to blow a horn,

199
00:15:20,139 --> 00:15:23,539
such as the Jews at least in Madina, that's what Jews would do.

200
00:15:24,632 --> 00:15:27,288
So, Abdullah Bin Zaidرضي الله عنه saw a dream,

201
00:15:28,471 --> 00:15:30,329
He saw a man carrying a bell.

202
00:15:30,440 --> 00:15:35,480
So, Abdullah Bin Zaid(عبدالله بن زيد) told him; O servant of Allah, how much would you sell that bell for?

203
00:15:36,301 --> 00:15:38,792
The man said; Why do you want it?

204
00:15:39,435 --> 00:15:42,419
Abdullah(عبدالله) said; to invite people to prayer.

205
00:15:43,389 --> 00:15:46,231
So, the man said; How about if I suggest something better?

206
00:15:46,683 --> 00:15:47,738
He said; What is it?

207
00:15:48,199 --> 00:15:49,899
He said; You say,

208
00:15:49,938 --> 00:15:51,304
 اللَّهُ أَكْبَرُ ، اللَّهُ أَكْبَرُ

209
00:15:51,478 --> 00:15:53,089
اللَّهُ أَكْبَرُ ، اللَّهُ أَكْبَرُ ،

210
00:15:54,222 --> 00:15:55,629
أَشْهَدُ أَنْ لا إِلَهَ إِلا اللَّهُ ،

211
00:15:55,669 --> 00:15:57,201
أَشْهَدُ أَنْ لا إِلَهَ إِلا اللَّهُ

212
00:15:57,772 --> 00:15:59,929
أَشْهَدُ أَنَّ مُحَمَّدًا رَسُولُ اللَّهِ

213
00:15:59,969 --> 00:16:02,263
أَشْهَدُ أَنَّ مُحَمَّدًا رَسُولُ اللَّهِ

214
00:16:02,658 --> 00:16:04,953
حَيَّ عَلَى الصَّلاةِ ، حَيَّ عَلَى الصَّلاةِ

215
00:16:05,406 --> 00:16:08,158
حَيَّ عَلَى الْفَلاحِ ، حَيَّ عَلَى الْفَلاحِ

216
00:16:08,752 --> 00:16:10,555
اللَّهُ أَكْبَرُ ، اللَّهُ أَكْبَرُ

217
00:16:10,848 --> 00:16:12,769
لا إِلَهَ إِلا اللَّهُ

218
00:16:14,332 --> 00:16:17,958
And then the man waited for a while and he came back to Abdullah(عبدالله) and said;

219
00:16:19,085 --> 00:16:21,204
And when you want to make Iqamah(إقامة), you say,

220
00:16:21,549 --> 00:16:23,359
اللَّهُ أَكْبَرُ ، اللَّهُ أَكْبَرُ

221
00:16:23,756 --> 00:16:27,542
أَشْهَدُ أَنْ لا إِلَهَ إِلا اللَّهُ ، أَشْهَدُ أَنَّ مُحَمَّدًا رَسُولُ اللَّهِ

222
00:16:28,137 --> 00:16:30,685
حَيَّ عَلَى الصَّلاةِ ،حَيَّ عَلَى الْفَلاحِ

223
00:16:30,930 --> 00:16:33,660
قَدْ قَامَت الصَّلَاةْ، قَدْ قَامَت الصَّلَاةْ

224
00:16:33,921 --> 00:16:35,814
اللَّهُ أَكْبَرُ ، اللَّهُ أَكْبَرُ

225
00:16:36,045 --> 00:16:37,919
لا إِلَهَ إِلَّا اللَّهُ

226
00:16:40,052 --> 00:16:44,125
So, Abdullah Bin Zaid(عبدالله بن زيد), immediately went to Rasool Allah ﷺ and told him about the dream.

227
00:16:44,294 --> 00:16:47,911
Rasool Allah ﷺ said: It is a good dream, In Sha Allah(ان شاءالله).

228
00:16:48,452 --> 00:16:49,355
رُوْيَا حَقْ

229
00:16:49,720 --> 00:16:51,156
This is a true dream.

230
00:16:51,910 --> 00:16:56,577
Go with Bilal(بلال), and teach this to him.

231
00:16:56,735 --> 00:16:58,741
Because his voice is better than yours.

232
00:16:59,443 --> 00:17:03,563
Abdullah Bin Zaid(عبدالله بن زيد) is one who gets the credit for the Adhaan(آذان).

233
00:17:03,683 --> 00:17:08,765
But Rasool Allah ﷺ did not allow him to make it, he told him to have Bilal(بلال) do it, because Bilal(بلال) has a better voice.

234
00:17:10,192 --> 00:17:17,812
So they both, went together and Abdullah Bin Zaid(عبدالله بن زيد) was teaching Bilal(بلال) the Adhaan(آذان) that he was taught in his dream.

235
00:17:19,562 --> 00:17:22,069
And when he finished, Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمر ابن الخطاب) came running.

236
00:17:22,188 --> 00:17:25,132
And he said: O Rasool Allah, I saw that dream.

237
00:17:26,362 --> 00:17:29,526
Rasool Allah ﷺ said: Al-Hamdolillah(ألحمدلله), Al-Hamdolillah(ألحمدلله).

238
00:17:31,012 --> 00:17:35,767
And this is an indication that it's a true dream, when more than one person sees the same dream,

239
00:17:36,156 --> 00:17:38,458
this an indication that it is a true dream.

240
00:17:40,072 --> 00:17:43,631
So, this is the story of Adhaan(آذان).

241
00:17:44,624 --> 00:17:49,486
And Adhaan(آذان) has became the most prominent symbol of Islam.

242
00:17:50,664 --> 00:17:55,210
Now a days, you know that you are in a Muslim country or Muslim town if you hear Adhaan(آذان)

243
00:17:56,012 --> 00:18:03,824
So, this is the most prominent expression of Islam, or it's the most outwardly or public symbol of Islam.

244
00:18:05,962 --> 00:18:08,018
What was the direction of Qibla(قبله) in the beginning.?

245
00:18:08,342 --> 00:18:14,449
The direction of Qibla(قبله) was towards the north, because they used to pray towards Jerusalem.

246
00:18:15,862 --> 00:18:17,283
A few months after Hijrah(هجرة),

247
00:18:17,841 --> 00:18:23,107
the Qibla(قبله) changed from the north towards the south, the exact opposite direction towards Makkah.

248
00:18:24,440 --> 00:18:29,604
In the direction of the old Qibla(قبله), they built a shed, a roof

249
00:18:29,755 --> 00:18:35,150
 that would provide shade, and the place under it would be called As-Suffah(ألصفه),

250
00:18:35,991 --> 00:18:37,104
it would be called As-Suffah(ألصفه).

251
00:18:37,373 --> 00:18:40,144
So what is As-Suffah(ألصفه) and who are Ahl-Us-Suffah(اهل الصفه).?

252
00:18:41,110 --> 00:18:43,960
The definition of As-Suffah(ألصفه), according to Ibn Hajar(ابن هجر) is;

253
00:18:43,985 --> 00:18:47,807
اَلصُّفَّهْ مَكَانٌ فِيْ مُؤَخِّرِ الْمٍسْجِدِ النَبْوِيْ

254
00:18:48,315 --> 00:18:55,251
 مُظلَّلْ اُعِدَّ لِنُزُوْلِ الْغُرْبَآءْ فِيْهِ مِمَّنْ لَّا مَأوى لَه’وَلَا أهل

255
00:18:55,669 --> 00:18:58,094
Ibn Hajar(ابن هجر) says; As-Suffah(ألصفه) is a place,

256
00:18:58,610 --> 00:19:02,275
at the back of Al-Masjid Al-Nabawi(مسجدالنبوي), and it is shaded

257
00:19:02,529 --> 00:19:10,027
and it was prepared for the foreigners, the ones who don'thave any family or any place to stay.

258
00:19:11,688 --> 00:19:12,726
And Abu Hurairah(ابوهريرة) says;

259
00:19:12,766 --> 00:19:18,887
وَاَهْلُ الصُّفَّةِ ضيَافُ الْاِسْلَامِ لَا يَأوُوْنَ عَلَى اَهْلٍ وَلَامَالٍ وَلَا عَلَى اَحَدْ

260
00:19:18,911 --> 00:19:19,866
And this is in Bukhari(بخاريْ),

261
00:19:20,163 --> 00:19:23,385
Abu Hurairah(ابوهريرة) says, about As-Suffah(ألصفه), and he was one of them.

262
00:19:23,710 --> 00:19:26,615
He says, As-Suffah(ألصفه) are the guests of Islam.

263
00:19:27,631 --> 00:19:32,489
They are the ones who don't have any family or wealth to fall back on.

264
00:19:33,538 --> 00:19:36,857
So they live in this place called As-Suffah(ألصفه).

265
00:19:38,070 --> 00:19:43,194
Now not everyone who lived there was forced to live there because of their condition,

266
00:19:43,219 --> 00:19:47,892
some of them chose, volunteered to join Ahlus-Suffah(اهل الصفه), such as Abu Hurairah(ابوهريرة)

267
00:19:48,542 --> 00:19:51,981
because it seems that Abu Hurairah(ابوهريرة) did have wealth when he made Hijrah(هجرة),

268
00:19:52,442 --> 00:19:59,947
but he chose to devote his time to studying and therefore he lived with the people of As-Suffah(ألصفه).

269
00:20:00,820 --> 00:20:02,023
He says about himself;

270
00:20:03,035 --> 00:20:07,159
اِنَّكُمْ تَقُوْلُوْنَ اِنَّ اَبَا هُرَيْرَهْ يُكْثِرُالْحَدِيْثَ اَلرَّسُوْلِ الله،

271
00:20:07,412 --> 00:20:12,836
وَتَقُوْلُوْنَ مَا بَال الْمُهَاجِرِيْنَ وَلْاَنْصَارْ لَا يُحَدِّثُوْنَ عَنْ رسول الله بِمِثْلِ حَدِيْثِ اَبُو هُرَيْرَه

272
00:20:13,256 --> 00:20:18,017
He said, some people are saying, how come Abu Hurairah(ابوهريرة) narrates a lot of Hadith(حديث),

273
00:20:18,331 --> 00:20:20,268
while Al-Muhajireen(المهاجرين) and Al-Ansaar(ألأنصار) don't.

274
00:20:20,762 --> 00:20:23,977
Now we know that Abu Hurairah(ابوهريرة) was late in becoming Muslim.

275
00:20:25,182 --> 00:20:28,970
So, how come he has narrated more Hadith(حديث) and everyone else.

276
00:20:29,672 --> 00:20:35,304
Abu Hurairah(ابوهريرة) is number one in terms of narrating Hadith(حديث) compared to all of the other Sahabah(صحابه).

277
00:20:35,329 --> 00:20:38,034
How come Abu Hurairah(ابوهريرة) knew more Ahadith(احاديث) than everybody else?

278
00:20:38,225 --> 00:20:42,248
So he says, he's giving us the explanation, he's giving us the reason. He said;

279
00:20:43,054 --> 00:20:48,114
وَاِنَّ اِخْوَةِ مِنَّ الْمُهَاجِرِيْنَ  كَانَ يَشْغَلُهُمْ صَفق الْاَسْوَاقِ

280
00:20:53,066 --> 00:20:53,066
وَكُنْتُ اَلْزَمُ رَسُوُلَ الله صلى الله عليه وسلم علَى مِلْءِ بَطْنِي،

281
00:20:53,516 --> 00:20:59,175
فأشْهَدُ إذَا غَابُوا، وأَحْفَظُ إذَا نَسُوا وكانَ يَشْغَلُ إخْوَتي مِنَ الأنْصَارِ

282
00:20:59,350 --> 00:21:05,390
عَمَلُ أمْوَالِهِمْ، وكُنْتُ امْرَأً مِسْكِينًا مِن مَسَاكِينِ الصُّفَّةِ، أعِي حِينَ يَنْسَوْنَ

283
00:21:05,870 --> 00:21:10,795
He said: My brothers from Al-Muhajireen(ألمهاجرين) were busy with business.

284
00:21:12,268 --> 00:21:15,459
While I used to follow Rasool Allah ﷺ on an empty stomach

285
00:21:15,802 --> 00:21:20,293
I had nothing I was poor, but I was still following Rasool Allah ﷺ all the time.

286
00:21:21,602 --> 00:21:27,337
So, I would attend, when they are absent, and I would remember when they would forget.

287
00:21:28,614 --> 00:21:32,395
And then he said; The Ansaar(أنصار), were busy with their farms,

288
00:21:32,887 --> 00:21:37,379
and I was a poor man and I would remember, what they wouldn't.

289
00:21:37,834 --> 00:21:40,580
Because he devoted his life to studying.

290
00:21:41,592 --> 00:21:45,020
He had time to review the Ahadith(أحاديث) that he would hear from Rasool Allah ﷺ.

291
00:21:45,060 --> 00:21:48,691
In fact, he says about himself that I split the night into three parts.

292
00:21:49,353 --> 00:21:51,229
One part, I would sleep one part, I would pray

293
00:21:51,269 --> 00:21:56,151
and one part, I would review the Ahadith(احاديث) of Rasool Allah ﷺ, that I would hear during the day,

294
00:21:56,743 --> 00:21:59,561
while the other Muhajireen Wal Ansaar(مهاجرين والأنصار) were busy, they had work to do.

295
00:21:59,823 --> 00:22:03,283
The Muhajireen(مهاجرين) had business and the Ansaar(أنْصَار) had farms.

296
00:22:03,804 --> 00:22:08,034
While Abu Hurairah(ابوهريرة) had nothing to preoccupy him from studying.

297
00:22:08,697 --> 00:22:15,115
So he chose to be among Ahl-Us-Suffah(اهل الصفه), so that he could go and study with Rasool Allah ﷺ full time.

298
00:22:17,154 --> 00:22:19,119
How would the people of As-Suffah(ألصفه) live.?

299
00:22:20,174 --> 00:22:24,441
One source of livelihood for them, was the Sadaqaat(صدقات) that Rasool Allah ﷺ would sent to them.

300
00:22:24,824 --> 00:22:28,347
When Rasool Allah ﷺ would receive Sadaqah(صدقه), he would send it to them.

301
00:22:29,042 --> 00:22:32,770
And when he would receive a gift, he would take some of it and give them the rest.

302
00:22:33,358 --> 00:22:36,205
Now the Sadaqah(صدقه) you notice that I didn't say that Rasool Ullah would take any of it

303
00:22:36,245 --> 00:22:39,285
because Rasool Allah ﷺ did not accept Sadaqah(صدقه).

304
00:22:40,488 --> 00:22:45,594
Rasool Allah ﷺ would encourage the well off Sahabah(صحابه) to invite them.

305
00:22:46,518 --> 00:22:50,228
One of the Ansaar(أنْصَار) Ya'eesh Al-Ghaffari(يعيش ألغفاري), he said;

306
00:22:50,268 --> 00:22:54,061
My father was from among the people of As-Suffah(ألصفه).

307
00:22:54,848 --> 00:23:01,557
Rasool Allah ﷺ ordered the Sahabah(صحابه) to invite Ahlus-Suffah(أهل الصفه) to their houses.

308
00:23:01,926 --> 00:23:08,432
So, they came and every one of these Sahabah(صحابه) took some of us away, until only five of us were left.

309
00:23:08,803 --> 00:23:13,563
And then Rasool Allah ﷺ told us all to go with him, to his house, and he fed us.

310
00:23:14,694 --> 00:23:22,264
And in another narration, Rasool Allah ﷺ says; Whoever has food enough for two people should take a third with him,

311
00:23:22,581 --> 00:23:28,826
and will have her has enough food for four people, he should take a fifth or sixth person with him.

312
00:23:29,868 --> 00:23:32,144
So, I just want to comment here and say that,

313
00:23:32,350 --> 00:23:36,933
you notice that sacrifice and generosity was part of Islam from various early on.

314
00:23:37,655 --> 00:23:39,367
In fact, from Makkah from day one,

315
00:23:40,281 --> 00:23:48,104
Allahعَزّوجَلّ has revealed Ayaat(آيات) about taking care of the orphan, taking care of the needy, being generous towards the guest.

316
00:23:48,511 --> 00:23:52,679
All of these are Ibadaat(عبادات) that were encouraged from day one.

317
00:23:53,171 --> 00:23:58,276
So, we shouldn't think that being a Muslim does not demand sacrifice.

318
00:23:58,639 --> 00:24:04,258
There's no free ride, if we want Jannah(جنة), if we seek to please Allahعَزّوجَلّ,

319
00:24:04,599 --> 00:24:12,523
we have to sacrifice for Allahعَزّوجَلّ, we have to give and giving was part of being a Muslim from day one.

320
00:24:12,952 --> 00:24:17,405
These Sahabah(صحابه) who were inviting others, they weren't millionaires.

321
00:24:17,452 --> 00:24:18,554
 Rasool Allah ﷺ was saying;

322
00:24:18,606 --> 00:24:22,784
if you have enough food for two people, only two people, you take a third person with you.

323
00:24:23,261 --> 00:24:28,582
So, he's telling the Sahabah(صحابه) to invite others to their houses, when they only have enough food for two people.

324
00:24:29,282 --> 00:24:35,560
Rasool Allah ﷺ would take care of them, even though others would come to him for needs.

325
00:24:36,991 --> 00:24:43,687
An example was Fatimaرضي الله عنها , the daughter of Rasool Allah ﷺ, the most beloved to the Messenger of Allah.

326
00:24:45,136 --> 00:24:49,816
She had to do all of the hard work at home

327
00:24:50,570 --> 00:24:54,957
until her hands were becoming injured, and coarse.

328
00:24:56,081 --> 00:25:01,988
So, Ali Ibn Abi Talib(علي ابن ابي طالب) told her that your father has received some savvy(سوي), savvy are slaves.

329
00:25:02,822 --> 00:25:05,168
So, go and ask him to give you a servant,

330
00:25:05,851 --> 00:25:09,605
so Fatimaرضي الله عنها goes to her father and asks for a servant.

331
00:25:10,681 --> 00:25:14,383
What does Rasool Allah ﷺ say to his most beloved.? What does he say to his daughter.?

332
00:25:14,652 --> 00:25:16,644
Whom he can see her suffering.

333
00:25:16,890 --> 00:25:17,632
He said;

334
00:25:18,151 --> 00:25:26,288
وَالله! لَا اُعْطِيْكُمْ وَأدع اَهْلُ الصُّفَّةِ  تَطْوِيْ بُطُوْنَهُمْ مِنَّ الْجُوْعِ لَا اَجِدُ مَااُنْفِقُ عَلَيْهِمْ

335
00:25:26,479 --> 00:25:30,063
وَلَكِنْ اَبِيْعَهُمْ وَاُنْفِق عَلَيْهِمْ اَثْمَانُهُمْ

336
00:25:31,031 --> 00:25:37,985
In the name of Allah, I am not going to give you and leave the people of As-Suffah(الصفه) with hungry stomachs

337
00:25:38,183 --> 00:25:40,219
because they don't have any money.

338
00:25:40,521 --> 00:25:43,473
And I don't have any money to spend on them.

339
00:25:43,846 --> 00:25:50,921
So, I'm going to sell these slaves and I'm going to use that money to give it to Ahlus Suffah(أهل الصفه).

340
00:25:51,641 --> 00:25:58,903
So, Rasool Allah ﷺ was giving Ahlus Suffah(أهل الصفه) and preventing his own daughter, Fatima رضي الله عنها ,

341
00:25:59,861 --> 00:26:03,820
that shows you how much Rasool Allah ﷺ cared for Ahlus Suffah(أهل الصفه).

342
00:26:04,630 --> 00:26:07,225
Now Ahlus Suffah(أهل الصفه), you know,

343
00:26:07,487 --> 00:26:12,257
we shouldn't think that Ahlus Suffah(أهل الصفه) are these people, who are trying to take advantage of all of the freebies

344
00:26:12,521 --> 00:26:15,669
free lodging and free food and, and they're just do nothing.

345
00:26:16,121 --> 00:26:18,184
These were very active people in Ibadah(عبادة).

346
00:26:19,091 --> 00:26:20,518
These were true monks.

347
00:26:21,211 --> 00:26:22,715
These were students of knowledge.

348
00:26:23,121 --> 00:26:26,554
These were scholars, these were Mujahideen(مجاهدين).

349
00:26:26,821 --> 00:26:28,432
Many of them became Shuhadaa(شهدآء).

350
00:26:28,841 --> 00:26:34,880
For example, among the scholars who graduated from the ranks of Ahlus Suffah(أهل الصفه) are the Abu Hurairahرضي الله عنه,

351
00:26:35,151 --> 00:26:38,980
the most prolific narrator of the Hadith(حديث) of Rasool Allah ﷺ.

352
00:26:39,911 --> 00:26:45,935
Another member of Ahlus Suffah(أهل الصفه) was Hudhaifa Bin Yaman(حزيفه بن يمان), the expert of the Ahadith(احاديث) of Fittan(فتن),

353
00:26:46,372 --> 00:26:49,838
 most of the Ahadith(احاديث) about the end of time came to us through who.?

354
00:26:50,186 --> 00:26:52,051
Hudhaifa Bin Yamanرضي الله عنه.

355
00:26:52,344 --> 00:26:56,619
And then for example, to talk about Shuhada'a(شهدآء) from among Ahlus Suffah(أهل الصفه),

356
00:26:56,770 --> 00:26:58,072
Safwaan Ibn Baidha'a(صفوان إبن بيضاء ),

357
00:26:58,333 --> 00:26:59,765
 Khareem Bin Fatiq Al-Asdi ( خريم بن فاتك الأسدي),

358
00:27:00,036 --> 00:27:01,183
Khabeeb Bin Isaaf(خبيب بن إساف),

359
00:27:01,341 --> 00:27:02,437
Saalim Bin Umair(سالم بن عمير),

360
00:27:02,588 --> 00:27:05,532
Harissa Bin Nouman(حارثه بن نعمان) were Shuhadaa(شهدآء) in Battle of Badr(بدر),

361
00:27:05,838 --> 00:27:09,583
Handhala(حنظله), the one who was washed by the angels was a Shaheed(شهيد) in Uhud(أحَد),

362
00:27:10,551 --> 00:27:14,818
Jurhud Bin Khuwailid(جرهد بن خويلد), Abu Suraiha Al-Ghifaari(أبو سريحه ألغفاري) became Shuhadaa(شهدآء) on Hudaybiyyah(حديبيه),

363
00:27:15,361 --> 00:27:19,372
Saqif Bin Amr(ساقف بن عمرو) became a Shaheed on Khaybar(خيبر),

364
00:27:19,728 --> 00:27:22,397
Abdullah Zulbajadain(عبدالله ذالبجادين) Shaheed(شهيد) on Tabook(تبوك),

365
00:27:22,722 --> 00:27:26,889
Salim Moula Abi Hudaifah(سالم مولا أبي حذيفه ), Zaid Bin Khattab(زيد بن خطاب), the brother of Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمر ابن الخطاب)

366
00:27:27,079 --> 00:27:28,898
were Shuhada'a(شهدآء) in Yamama(يمامه).

367
00:27:30,098 --> 00:27:32,396
And they used to try to make a living, if they could.

368
00:27:32,936 --> 00:27:38,824
Zamakhshari(زمخشري) says that they used to gather, they used to collect the date seeds

369
00:27:39,260 --> 00:27:42,395
and they would crush them and then sell it as animal feed.

370
00:27:43,013 --> 00:27:46,272
So, they would try to make a living but the conditions were difficult,

371
00:27:46,609 --> 00:27:48,794
the conditions in Madina in general were difficult.

372
00:27:49,024 --> 00:27:51,127
So, they were forced into poverty.

373
00:27:51,353 --> 00:27:52,713
What was the number of Ahlus Suffah(أهل الصفه)?

374
00:27:53,323 --> 00:27:56,108
Well, the number goes up and down depending on the conditions,

375
00:27:56,823 --> 00:27:58,555
but they would average about 70.

376
00:27:58,920 --> 00:28:01,357
So, we're talking about a huge group of people

377
00:28:01,535 --> 00:28:06,222
and they used to live full time, in the back of Al-Masjid Al-Nabwi(مسجدالنبوي).

378
00:28:08,047 --> 00:28:09,613
They were very active in study

379
00:28:09,867 --> 00:28:15,228
because they were close to the center of learning, Al-Masjid Al-Nabwi(مسجدالنبوي), which was the University of Islam

380
00:28:15,873 --> 00:28:19,379
and that's why they have narrated a lot of a Ahadith(احاديث).

381
00:28:20,163 --> 00:28:23,216
Some points regarding Ahlus Suffah(أهل الصفه),

382
00:28:23,413 --> 00:28:27,269
number one, the importance of having a social welfare system.

383
00:28:28,133 --> 00:28:31,970
People would stay at As-Suffah(الصفه) and feed at the houses of Al-Ansaar(الأنْصَار).

384
00:28:32,517 --> 00:28:38,025
So, the Ansaarرضي الله عنهم, as we mentioned would invite them and take them to their houses,

385
00:28:38,078 --> 00:28:43,154
 and Rasool Allah ﷺ did the same, Abu Bakr(ابوبكر), Umar(عُمَر) Uthman(عثمان) the well off Muhajireen(مهاجرين) would do the same.

386
00:28:43,375 --> 00:28:46,114
So it's important to have this welfare system.

387
00:28:47,098 --> 00:28:48,543
And it's also part of Da'wah(دعوة).

388
00:28:49,059 --> 00:28:51,231
 Ubadah Bin Samitرضي الله عنه said;

389
00:28:51,513 --> 00:28:53,789
كَانَ رَسُوْلَ الله صلى الله عليه وسلم يُشْغَلْ

390
00:28:54,652 --> 00:29:03,138
Rasool Allah ﷺ would become busy, so he would turn over the new Muslims to us.

391
00:29:03,630 --> 00:29:10,634
فَاِذَا قَدِمَ رَجُلٌ مُهَاجِر عَلَى رَسُوْل الله صلى الله عليه وسلم دَفْعَه’ اِلَى رَجُلِ مِّنَّا  يُعَلِّمُهُ الْقُرْآنْ

392
00:29:11,170 --> 00:29:16,482
If a new Mohajir(مهاجر) immigrant would come to Rasool Allah ﷺ, this is a new Muslim, who just came into Madina,

393
00:29:16,818 --> 00:29:19,292
if he comes to Rasool Allah ﷺ and Rasool Allah was busy.

394
00:29:19,506 --> 00:29:23,490
He would send him, over to one of us, to teach him Qur'an.

395
00:29:24,382 --> 00:29:27,417
فَدَفَعَ اِلَيَّ رَسول الله صلى الله عليه وسلم رَجُلً

396
00:29:27,551 --> 00:29:30,061
So, Rasool Allah sent to me a man.

397
00:29:30,721 --> 00:29:32,407
وَكَانَ مَعَيْ فِيْ الْبَيْتْ

398
00:29:32,626 --> 00:29:34,694
وَعشِيْهِ عشَاء اَهْلِ الْبَيْتْ

399
00:29:34,970 --> 00:29:39,901
So, he stayed with me at home and I would feed him as a member of my own family.

400
00:29:40,679 --> 00:29:42,206
وَكُنْتُ اُقْرِءُه’الْقُرْآنَ

401
00:29:42,246 --> 00:29:43,645
And then I would teach him Qur'an.

402
00:29:44,119 --> 00:29:51,889
So, Da'wah(دعوة) to them also involved taking care of these new Muslims, who couldn't afford, Madina.

403
00:29:52,082 --> 00:29:54,114
Because some of them would make Hijrah(هجرة) to Madina

404
00:29:54,655 --> 00:29:57,722
and they would leave all of their wealth behind, these could be wealthy people,

405
00:29:58,084 --> 00:30:01,174
but they sacrificed everything for Allahعَزّوجَلّ and they came to Madina.

406
00:30:01,466 --> 00:30:04,475
So, it's now the responsibility of the Muslims to takecare of them.

407
00:30:04,667 --> 00:30:06,241
So, Ubadah(عبادة) is saying that

408
00:30:06,675 --> 00:30:12,260
Rasool Ullah send this man over to him to teach him Qur'an, but he also had to take care of his social needs.

409
00:30:12,695 --> 00:30:14,439
And this is very important in Da'wah(دعوة),

410
00:30:14,542 --> 00:30:17,963
sometimes we have people, who come from poor backgrounds would becoming Muslim.

411
00:30:18,205 --> 00:30:23,417
Sometimes they have people who had to give up their work because it's Haraam(حرام)

412
00:30:23,952 --> 00:30:29,802
and then they have nothing, it is a duty of the Muslims to be generous towards them

413
00:30:30,047 --> 00:30:34,401
and to take care of them in their first steps towards Allahعَزّوجَلّ.

414
00:30:35,542 --> 00:30:36,602
Number two,

415
00:30:36,967 --> 00:30:43,043
Rasool Allah ﷺ wanted the Muslim Jama'ah(جماعة), the Muslim society to become organized.

416
00:30:43,559 --> 00:30:47,808
So, he appointed representatives over these groups.

417
00:30:48,263 --> 00:30:50,938
So, Abu Hurairahرضي الله عنه was a Areef(عريف),

418
00:30:51,192 --> 00:30:57,029
Areef(عريف) is someone who would represent his people and would know them,

419
00:30:57,425 --> 00:31:00,780
and would express their needs towards the leader.

420
00:31:01,475 --> 00:31:05,044
So, Abu Hurairahرضي الله عنه was representative of Ahlus Suffah(اهل الصفه).

421
00:31:05,837 --> 00:31:12,036
So, if Rasool Allah ﷺ, had any instructions to give to Ahlus Suffah(اهلالصفه), or he wanted to hear their needs,

422
00:31:12,157 --> 00:31:16,593
it would occur through their representative, Abu Hurairahرضي الله عنه.

423
00:31:16,728 --> 00:31:22,437
 And this shows you the organization that Rasool Allah ﷺ instilled in the Muslim Jama'ah(جماعة).

424
00:31:23,595 --> 00:31:28,930
So, it's important that we organize our Muslim communities wherever we are,

425
00:31:29,485 --> 00:31:31,527
we organize according to the need.

426
00:31:32,915 --> 00:31:43,035
Now, we talked about the first project sponsored by Rasool Allah ﷺ, in Madina, and that was Al-Masjid(المسجد).

427
00:31:43,895 --> 00:31:45,281
What are the other three?

428
00:31:45,359 --> 00:31:51,428
Because Rasool Allah ﷺ embarked on four projects, as soon as he came into Madina.

429
00:31:51,832 --> 00:31:54,039
The first one was Al-Masjid Al-Nabawi(المسجدالنبوي).

430
00:31:54,535 --> 00:32:00,049
The second one was the establishing of brotherhood between Al-Muhajireen Al-Ansaar(المهاجرين والأنْصَار).

431
00:32:00,645 --> 00:32:07,846
The third was the covenant that would govern the relationships between the different communities in Madina,

432
00:32:07,945 --> 00:32:13,451
the Arabs and the Jews, and the foreign relations with the people of Quraish(قُرَيْشْ).

433
00:32:13,689 --> 00:32:16,672
And number four, the establishment of the Muslim army.

434
00:32:16,873 --> 00:32:23,661
These are the first four projects that Rasool Allah ﷺ embarked on, when he immigrated to Madina.

435
00:32:24,099 --> 00:32:27,928
We talked about the first one, the Masjid(مسجد), now we move on to the second.

436
00:32:29,297 --> 00:32:31,200
Brotherhood is very important in Islam.

437
00:32:32,105 --> 00:32:34,264
Allahعَزّوجَلّ, says;

438
00:32:34,554 --> 00:32:40,751
وَاعْتَصِمُوا بِحَبْلِ اللَّهِ جَمِيعًا وَلَا تَفَرَّقُوا ۚ

439
00:32:41,065 --> 00:32:52,148
وَاذْكُرُوا نِعْمَتَ اللَّهِ عَلَيْكُمْ إِذْ كُنْتُمْ أَعْدَاءً فَأَلَّفَ بَيْنَ قُلُوبِكُمْ فَأَصْبَحْتُمْ

440
00:32:52,474 --> 00:32:57,013
فَأَصْبَحْتُمْ بِنِعْمَتِهِ إِخْوَانًا

441
00:32:57,244 --> 00:33:05,731
وَكُنْتُمْ عَلَىٰ شَفَا حُفْرَةٍ مِنَ النَّارِ فَأَنْقَذَكُمْ مِنْهَا ۗ

442
00:33:06,004 --> 00:33:13,437
كَذَٰلِكَ يُبَيِّنُ اللَّهُ لَكُمْ آيَاتِهِ لَعَلَّكُمْ تَهْتَدُونَ۝

443
00:33:13,834 --> 00:33:17,343
And hold firmly to the rope of Allah all together

444
00:33:17,972 --> 00:33:19,555
and do not become divided.

445
00:33:20,772 --> 00:33:25,374
And remember the favor of Allah upon you, when you were enemies,

446
00:33:25,762 --> 00:33:27,750
and He brought your hearts together,

447
00:33:28,092 --> 00:33:30,426
and you became by His favor brothers

448
00:33:31,339 --> 00:33:33,640
and you were on the edge of a pit of the fire,

449
00:33:34,262 --> 00:33:35,597
and He saved you from it.

450
00:33:36,312 --> 00:33:40,614
Thus does Allah make clear to you, His verses that you may be guided.

451
00:33:41,862 --> 00:33:43,673
And Allahعَزّوجَلّ also says;

452
00:33:43,841 --> 00:33:46,844
وَأَلَّفَ بَيْنَ قُلُوبِهِمْ ۚ

453
00:33:47,083 --> 00:33:56,161
لَوْ أَنْفَقْتَ مَا فِي الْأَرْضِ جَمِيعًا مَا أَلَّفْتَ بَيْنَ قُلُوبِهِمْ

454
00:33:56,549 --> 00:34:05,049
وَلَٰكِنَّ اللَّهَ أَلَّفَ بَيْنَهُمْ ۚ إِنَّهُ عَزِيزٌ حَكِيمٌ۝

455
00:34:05,647 --> 00:34:07,819
And brought together their hearts

456
00:34:08,171 --> 00:34:14,042
If you have spent all that is in the earth you could not have brought their hearts together.

457
00:34:14,481 --> 00:34:16,066
But Allah brought them together.

458
00:34:16,382 --> 00:34:19,513
Indeed, He is Exalted in Might and Wise.

459
00:34:19,910 --> 00:34:25,623
Allahعَزّوجَلّ is telling Muhammadﷺ that it is Allah, Who brought the hearts of the Muslims together.

460
00:34:25,901 --> 00:34:28,419
 And if you spent all the money in the world you couldn't have done so,

461
00:34:28,975 --> 00:34:31,815
you cannot buy off the hearts of men.

462
00:34:32,251 --> 00:34:34,216
This was a favor from Allahعَزّوجَلّ

463
00:34:34,438 --> 00:34:38,509
that He brought Al-Muhajireen(المهاجرين) and Al-Ansaar(الأنْصَار) together and made them brothers.

464
00:34:40,322 --> 00:34:42,273
Allahعَزّوجَلّ says about Al-Ansaar(الأنْصَار);

465
00:34:42,430 --> 00:34:51,377
وَالَّذِينَ تَبَوَّءُو الدَّارَ وَالْإِيمَانَ مِنْ قَبْلِهِمْ يُحِبُّونَ مَنْ هَاجَرَ إِلَيْهِمْ

466
00:34:51,711 --> 00:35:01,674
يُحِبُّونَ مَنْ هَاجَرَ إِلَيْهِمْ وَلَا يَجِدُونَ فِي صُدُورِهِمْ حَاجَةً مِمَّا أُوتُوا

467
00:35:02,229 --> 00:35:09,170
وَيُؤْثِرُونَ عَلَىٰ أَنْفُسِهِمْ وَلَوْ كَانَ بِهِمْ خَصَاصَةٌ ۚ

468
00:35:09,615 --> 00:35:16,647
وَمَنْ يُوقَ شُحَّ نَفْسِهِ فَأُولَٰئِكَ هُمُ الْمُفْلِحُونَ۝

469
00:35:17,364 --> 00:35:22,280
And those who were settled in the home and adopted the faith before them,

470
00:35:23,059 --> 00:35:25,196
they love those who immigrated to them.

471
00:35:25,273 --> 00:35:29,167
 So, this is the first quality of Al-Ansaar(الأنْصَار), they settled in their home, Madina.

472
00:35:29,942 --> 00:35:33,472
Their second quality, they love those who immigrated to them.

473
00:35:34,743 --> 00:35:38,035
So, they don't feel that these guests are burden on them.

474
00:35:38,622 --> 00:35:41,265
They loved Al-Muhajireen(اَلمهاجرين).

475
00:35:42,999 --> 00:35:50,355
The third quality, and find not any want in their breasts of what they were given,

476
00:35:51,349 --> 00:35:54,611
the fourth quality but give them preference over themselves,

477
00:35:54,724 --> 00:35:58,592
Al-Ansaar(الأنْصَار) would give the Muhajireen(مهاجرين) preference over themselves,

478
00:35:58,993 --> 00:36:01,315
even though they are in privation.

479
00:36:02,738 --> 00:36:09,346
And whoever is protected from the stinginess of his soul, it is those who would be successful.

480
00:36:09,985 --> 00:36:13,725
Allahسبحانه تعالى has protected Al-Ansaar(الأنْصَار) from stinginess in their souls.

481
00:36:16,186 --> 00:36:18,376
This Ayaat(آيات) are talking about Brotherhood in general,

482
00:36:18,408 --> 00:36:22,297
but there's a specific brotherhood that we're talking about here.

483
00:36:22,916 --> 00:36:25,919
And that is the Brotherhood between the Al-Muhajireen(المهاجرين), Al-Ansaar(الأنْصَار)

484
00:36:26,511 --> 00:36:28,711
which started according to Al-Sohaili(ألسهيلي),

485
00:36:29,648 --> 00:36:34,718
he said: Some people say that this pact of brotherhood started five months after Hijrah(هجرة),

486
00:36:35,283 --> 00:36:37,391
while some say nine months after Hijrah(هجرة),

487
00:36:37,637 --> 00:36:42,592
while some say it was established as soon as he built Al-Masjid Al-Nabwi(المسجدالنبوي),

488
00:36:42,695 --> 00:36:45,744
so we're talking about immediately as he set in, in Madina.

489
00:36:46,883 --> 00:36:49,041
What this brotherhood entailed is.

490
00:36:49,636 --> 00:36:53,970
They were brothers just as if they were Blood Brothers, meaning that even in inheritance,

491
00:36:54,883 --> 00:36:59,063
the rules of inheritance would apply to them, just as if they were blood brothers.

492
00:37:00,482 --> 00:37:06,061
An example of one of these brotherhood relationships between Al-Muhajir(المهاجر) and Al-Ansaar(الأنْصَار)

493
00:37:06,442 --> 00:37:09,075
was that of Saad Ibn Rabiyaah(سعدابن ربيعه) and Abdur Rahman Bin Auf(عبدالرحمن بن عوف).

494
00:37:10,243 --> 00:37:13,213
Abdur Rahman Bin Auf(عبدالرحمن بن عوف) was a Muhajir(مهاجر) from Makkah.

495
00:37:13,293 --> 00:37:16,126
He's one of the 10 who are given the glad tidings of Jannah(جنة).

496
00:37:16,608 --> 00:37:18,468
He stayed at the house of Saad Ibn Rabiyaah(سعدابن ربيعه).

497
00:37:19,933 --> 00:37:23,106
Saad Ibn Rabiyaah(سعدابن ربيعه) told him, O, my brother,

498
00:37:23,668 --> 00:37:27,151
I am one of the most wealthiest men in Madina.

499
00:37:28,229 --> 00:37:31,860
I will split my wealth in half and give it to you.

500
00:37:32,793 --> 00:37:36,343
And I'm married to two women, you can take a look at both of them

501
00:37:36,453 --> 00:37:38,240
and choose whichever one you want.

502
00:37:38,542 --> 00:37:42,637
And I will divorce her and after she finishes her Iddat(عدة) you can marry her.

503
00:37:43,804 --> 00:37:46,853
This is the level of sacrifice, that they were willing to go to.

504
00:37:48,103 --> 00:37:50,033
Abdur Rahman Bin Aufرضي الله عنه said;

505
00:37:50,476 --> 00:37:52,277
بَارَكَ اللهُ لَكَ فِيْ اَهْلِكَ وَمَالِكْ

506
00:37:52,384 --> 00:37:54,447
May Allah bless your wealth and bless your family.

507
00:37:56,099 --> 00:37:58,506
Show me the way to the market.

508
00:37:58,712 --> 00:38:05,051
So, he said, thank you, You can keep your wealth, and may Allah bless it for you and bless your family.

509
00:38:05,856 --> 00:38:09,703
But I want you to show me the way towards the market.

510
00:38:11,369 --> 00:38:15,042
Saad Ibn Rabiyaah(سعدابن ربيعه) did show him the way towards the market of Bannu Qainuqah(بنو قينقاع).

511
00:38:15,906 --> 00:38:19,028
Abdur Rahman Bin Auf(عبدالرحمن بن عوف) Allahسبحانه وتعالى has blessed his wealth.

512
00:38:19,980 --> 00:38:24,536
So, very early on, he was able to establish himself,

513
00:38:25,541 --> 00:38:28,624
and he became very wealthy.

514
00:38:29,696 --> 00:38:31,962
He went in the market and he worked and he made some money.

515
00:38:32,766 --> 00:38:39,455
One day Rasool Allah ﷺ saw on him, some yellow color, Sufrah(صفراء).

516
00:38:39,764 --> 00:38:44,828
This was a type of powder that women would use as makeup, in Madina.

517
00:38:45,866 --> 00:38:50,323
So, it was on the face of Abdur Rahman Bin Auf(عبدالرحمن بن عوف) women's makeup was on his face.

518
00:38:51,076 --> 00:38:53,362
So, Rasool Allah ﷺ told him;ما هذا, What is this?

519
00:38:54,037 --> 00:38:55,123
Did you get married?

520
00:38:55,426 --> 00:38:57,167
Abdur Rahman Bin Auf(عبدالرحمن بن عوف) said: yes.

521
00:38:57,571 --> 00:39:00,897
So, Rasool Allah ﷺ asked him and what did you give her as Mahar(مهر)?

522
00:39:01,426 --> 00:39:02,701
Where did you get the money from?

523
00:39:03,206 --> 00:39:09,075
Abdur Rahman Bin Auf(عبدالرحمن بن عوف) said: I gave her the size of a date seed, in gold as her Mahar(مهر).

524
00:39:09,176 --> 00:39:11,052
So, he has already enough money to buy gold.

525
00:39:12,103 --> 00:39:13,769
Rasool Allah ﷺ, then told him;

526
00:39:13,812 --> 00:39:14,949
أَوْلِمْ وَلَوْ بِشَاءْ

527
00:39:15,003 --> 00:39:19,130
Make a Valimah(وليمه), even if you only slaughter one goat or one Sheep.

528
00:39:21,413 --> 00:39:23,596
These brothers would also advise each other.

529
00:39:24,203 --> 00:39:30,102
An example of that is the Brotherhood between Salman Al-Farisi(سلمان الفارسي) and Abu Dardaرضي الله عنه.

530
00:39:31,391 --> 00:39:33,964
Abu Darda(أبو درداء) was a Abid(عابد),

531
00:39:34,703 --> 00:39:37,163
he was a worshipper of Allah and he was a Zahid(زاهد).

532
00:39:38,552 --> 00:39:41,910
Salman Farisiرضي الله عنه came in, and this was before Hijab(حجاب),

533
00:39:42,741 --> 00:39:46,067
And he saw that his wife wasn't taking care of herself,

534
00:39:46,931 --> 00:39:48,916
in her dress, in the way she looks.

535
00:39:50,178 --> 00:39:52,344
 So, Salman(سلمان) told her What's wrong with you?

536
00:39:52,963 --> 00:39:56,731
He is speaking to the wife of Abu Darda(أبو درداء) and telling her because she was Muttabazzila(متبذله),

537
00:39:56,771 --> 00:39:59,675
Muttabazzila(متبذله) means, she didn't take care of her looks.

538
00:40:00,513 --> 00:40:01,903
So, Salman(سلمان) is asking her, Why?

539
00:40:02,379 --> 00:40:07,399
She said: Because your brother Abu Darda(أبو درداء) isn't interested in Duniya(دنيا).

540
00:40:08,543 --> 00:40:11,223
Your brother Abu Darda(أبو درداء) isn't interested in Duniyah(دُنِيَّا).

541
00:40:12,036 --> 00:40:15,975
So, there was no need for her to look good in front of her husband.

542
00:40:16,433 --> 00:40:19,353
Because he wasn't really interested, in anything regarding this world.

543
00:40:20,702 --> 00:40:24,564
So, Salman Al-Farisi(سلمان الفارسي), when Abu Darda(أبو درداء) came in,

544
00:40:24,763 --> 00:40:27,989
 Abu Darda(أبو درداء) brought him some food, and told Salman(سلمان) to eat.

545
00:40:29,643 --> 00:40:31,590
And he said, I am fasting.

546
00:40:32,027 --> 00:40:35,396
Salman(سلمان) told him; I'm not going to eat until, you also eat with me.

547
00:40:35,539 --> 00:40:39,007
So, he forced Abu Darda(أبو درداء) to break his fasting.

548
00:40:39,853 --> 00:40:45,758
And then when night came Abu Darda(أبو درداء) stood up to start his Qayaam Ul Lail(قيام اليل),

549
00:40:46,210 --> 00:40:47,821
Salman(سلمان) told him; Go and sleep.

550
00:40:48,885 --> 00:40:49,774
So, he slept.

551
00:40:50,723 --> 00:40:53,438
And then he woke up and he wanted to pray, Salman(سلمان) told him; Go and sleep.

552
00:40:54,253 --> 00:40:59,301
And then towards the end of the night, Salman(سلمان) went to Abu Darda(أبو درداء) and told him: Now, you can pray.

553
00:41:00,412 --> 00:41:05,072
Abu Darda(أبو درداء) the next day, went to Rasool Allah ﷺ and told him, I mean this man had me break my fast

554
00:41:05,175 --> 00:41:06,913
and he had me sleep at night.

555
00:41:07,587 --> 00:41:08,706
Rasool Allah ﷺ told him;

556
00:41:08,785 --> 00:41:09,643
صَدَقَ سلمان,

557
00:41:09,714 --> 00:41:10,675
Salman(سلمان) was right.

558
00:41:10,951 --> 00:41:11,919
 Salman(سلمان) said;

559
00:41:12,793 --> 00:41:15,863
He told Abu Darda(أبو درداء) and this was conveyed to Rasool Allah ﷺ, he said;

560
00:41:16,324 --> 00:41:18,352
اِنَّ لِنَفْسِكَ عَلَيْكَ حَقَّا،

561
00:41:19,034 --> 00:41:21,192
 وَاِنَّ لِاَهْلِكَ عَلَيْكَ حَقَّا،

562
00:41:21,558 --> 00:41:23,278
وَاِنَّ لِرَبِّكَ عَلَيْكَ حَقَّا

563
00:41:23,886 --> 00:41:25,489
اِنَّ لِرَبِّكَ عَلَيْكَ حَقَّا

564
00:41:26,220 --> 00:41:28,105
You have obligations towards Allah.

565
00:41:28,594 --> 00:41:30,092
واِنَّ لِنَفْسِكَ عَلَيْكَ حَقَّا

566
00:41:30,132 --> 00:41:32,229
And you have obligations towards yourself

567
00:41:32,726 --> 00:41:34,172
وَاِنَّ لِاَهْلِكَ عَلَيْكَ حَقَّا

568
00:41:34,236 --> 00:41:36,402
And you have obligations towards your family.

569
00:41:36,645 --> 00:41:38,519
فَاَعْطِ كُلَّ ذِيْ حَقٍ حَقَّه

570
00:41:38,579 --> 00:41:41,347
So, fulfill the obligations of everyone?

571
00:41:42,584 --> 00:41:46,564
Salman Al-Farisi(سلمان الفارسي) here is, giving Naseeha(نصيحه) to Abu Darda(أبو درداء).

572
00:41:47,000 --> 00:41:49,024
Because Salman Al-Farsi(سلمان الفارسي) is more knowledgeable.

573
00:41:49,246 --> 00:41:52,133
The Muhajireen(مهاجرين) spent years with Rasool Allah ﷺ,

574
00:41:52,550 --> 00:41:54,479
and they have acquired all of this knowledge.

575
00:41:55,734 --> 00:42:01,290
Just want to note here that, Salman Al-Farisi(سلمان الفارسي) was a Mohajir(مهاجر) to Madina,

576
00:42:01,627 --> 00:42:07,453
in a sense that he, came from Persia to Madina for the sake of finding the Prophet,

577
00:42:08,088 --> 00:42:12,147
but he didn't come from Makkah, Salman Al-Farisi(سلمان الفارسي) came from Persia.

578
00:42:12,766 --> 00:42:19,482
But he was the brother of Abu Darda(أبو درداء) they were both made brothers by Rasool Allah ﷺ.

579
00:42:20,563 --> 00:42:25,224
So, the Ansaar(أنْصَار) were very cooperative and sacrificing towards Al-Muhajiroon(ألمهاجرون)

580
00:42:25,264 --> 00:42:27,984
In fact, Al-Ansaar(الأنْصَار), they went to Rasool Allah ﷺ and said;

581
00:42:28,401 --> 00:42:30,799
اِقْسِمْ بَيْنَنَا وَبَيْنَنَا اِخْوَانِ نَّخِيء

582
00:42:31,532 --> 00:42:38,006
O Messenger of Allah, split the palm groves between us and the Muhajireen(مهاجرين).

583
00:42:38,625 --> 00:42:42,359
They were offering Al-Muhajiroon(ألمهاجرون), half of their wealth.

584
00:42:43,727 --> 00:42:45,423
Rasool Allah ﷺ said: No.

585
00:42:45,995 --> 00:42:47,169
So the Ansaar(أنْصَار) said;

586
00:42:47,555 --> 00:42:50,727
تَكْفُوْنَنَا الْمُؤنة وَنُشْرِكُكُمْ فِيْ الثَّمَرَ

587
00:42:50,887 --> 00:42:57,838
Then you take care of the work, in the farms and we will split the harvest between us and you.

588
00:42:58,773 --> 00:43:02,046
Rasool Allah ﷺ agreed. And that was the deal,

589
00:43:02,276 --> 00:43:08,590
that the Muhajiroon(ألمهاجرون) will serve in their farms and then they would split the harvest in half.

590
00:43:09,287 --> 00:43:10,779
But even that didn't happen,

591
00:43:10,811 --> 00:43:14,033
the Ansaar(أنْصَار), even though they said, that will have the Muhajireen(مهاجرين) work.

592
00:43:14,120 --> 00:43:15,670
They ended up doing most of the work.

593
00:43:16,679 --> 00:43:17,906
So, Al-Muhajiroon(ألمهاجرون) said;

594
00:43:18,221 --> 00:43:25,365
يَا رَسُوْل الله، مَا رَاَيْنَا مِثْلَ قَوْمٍ قَدِمْنَا عَلَيْهِمْ اَحْسَنَ مُواسَاتٍ فِيْ قَلِيْلٍ،

595
00:43:25,587 --> 00:43:27,563
وَلَا اَحْسَنَ بَذلا فِيْ كَثِيْرٍ

596
00:43:27,793 --> 00:43:33,756
وَلَقَدْ كَفَوْنَا الْمُؤنَة وَ اَشْرَكُوْنَا  فِيْ الْمَهْنَة، حَتَّى لَقَدْ حَسِبْنَا اَنْ يَذْهَبُوا بِالْاَجْرِ كُلَّه

597
00:43:34,313 --> 00:43:36,264
The Muhajiroon(ألمهاجرون) came to Rasool Allah ﷺ and said;

598
00:43:36,319 --> 00:43:39,541
O Messenger of Allah! We have never seen a people like this.

599
00:43:40,089 --> 00:43:42,542
They comfort us, when they are poor

600
00:43:43,079 --> 00:43:45,653
and they are generous, when they are well off.

601
00:43:46,571 --> 00:43:51,217
They work in their forms, and then they split the harvest with us.

602
00:43:52,642 --> 00:43:57,399
We think that they would get all of the reward on the day of Judgment and leave us with nothing.

603
00:43:58,140 --> 00:44:04,048
Rasool Allah ﷺ said: No, As long as you are grateful towards them and as long as you make Dua(دُعَا) for them.

604
00:44:05,215 --> 00:44:11,037
As long as you are grateful and this shows you the value of being grateful to Allah and to His creation.

605
00:44:11,434 --> 00:44:14,215
Anybody who does us good, we should be grateful towards them.

606
00:44:14,746 --> 00:44:17,712
Otherwise they'll end up taking all of the Ajr(أجر) and leave us without anything.

607
00:44:18,568 --> 00:44:20,172
And make Dua(دُعَا) for them.

608
00:44:20,458 --> 00:44:24,156
And this is a habit that we should develop,

609
00:44:24,690 --> 00:44:26,323
If someone does you good, make Dua(دُعَا) for them.

610
00:44:26,950 --> 00:44:29,276
If someone has done you a favor make Dua(دُعَا) for them.

611
00:44:29,796 --> 00:44:33,646
Ask Allah سبحانه وتعالى and ask Allah with, you know, with sincerity,

612
00:44:33,671 --> 00:44:35,539
I mean sometimes we just do Dua(دُعَا),

613
00:44:35,981 --> 00:44:39,108
we just do it with the tongue and we don't really know what we're saying.

614
00:44:39,148 --> 00:44:41,302
O Jaza Kallah Khairen(جزاك الله خيراً), O Jaza Kallah Khairen(جزاك الله خيراً).

615
00:44:41,576 --> 00:44:45,498
But we have to do it, say it sincerely, may Allah reward you

616
00:44:45,836 --> 00:44:47,180
may Allahعَزّوجَلّ bless you,

617
00:44:47,220 --> 00:44:48,498
may Allahعَزّوجَلّ give you,

618
00:44:48,823 --> 00:44:51,021
may Allah give you Hasanah(حسنه) in this world

619
00:44:51,061 --> 00:44:52,633
 and give you Hasanah(حسنه) inthe afterlife.

620
00:44:53,173 --> 00:44:54,430
This is part of becoming Muslim.

621
00:44:54,477 --> 00:44:56,226
لَا يَشْكُرُالنَّاسْ لَا يَشْكُرُالله

622
00:44:56,620 --> 00:45:00,038
The one who's not grateful towards people is not going to be grateful towards Allah.

623
00:45:00,479 --> 00:45:09,097
This relationship of brotherhood was in pairs, I mean, one Muhajiri(مهاجري) and one Ansaar(أنْصَار) carried on for a while,

624
00:45:09,470 --> 00:45:13,114
 until the situation of the Muhajiroon(مهاجرون) improved.

625
00:45:13,490 --> 00:45:15,385
And then it was dissolved,

626
00:45:16,020 --> 00:45:18,393
and the general brotherhood of the Ummah(امة) remained.

627
00:45:18,712 --> 00:45:22,358
So, this specific type of brotherhood was dissolved,

628
00:45:22,656 --> 00:45:27,528
and inheritance laws now only applied to the blood relatives.

629
00:45:28,115 --> 00:45:29,227
Allahعَزّوجَلّ says;

630
00:45:29,711 --> 00:45:40,186
وَالَّذِينَ آمَنُوا مِنْ بَعْدُ وَهَاجَرُوا وَجَاهَدُوا مَعَكُمْ فَأُولَٰئِكَ مِنْكُمْ ۚ

631
00:45:40,567 --> 00:45:48,235
وَأُولُو الْأَرْحَامِ بَعْضُهُمْ أَوْلَىٰ بِبَعْضٍ فِي كِتَابِ اللَّهِ ۗ

632
00:45:48,553 --> 00:45:54,452
إِنَّ اللَّهَ بِكُلِّ شَيْءٍ عَلِيمٌ۝

633
00:45:55,248 --> 00:46:02,268
And those who believed after the initial immigration and immigrated and fought with you, they are of you.

634
00:46:02,633 --> 00:46:08,284
But those of blood relationship are more entitled to inheritance in the decree of Allah.

635
00:46:08,553 --> 00:46:10,847
Indeed, Allah is knowing of all things.

636
00:46:12,024 --> 00:46:15,226
One lesson to learn from this, topic of brotherhood,

637
00:46:16,064 --> 00:46:20,812
A new community was being developed based on a new bond.

638
00:46:21,690 --> 00:46:26,337
In Arabia, the bonds that existed were the bonds of blood relationship,

639
00:46:27,030 --> 00:46:29,895
the bonds of economical relationships,

640
00:46:29,973 --> 00:46:36,900
but now, a nation is born based on faith, it was a faith based community.

641
00:46:37,890 --> 00:46:40,764
We talked about the complication of the situation in Madina.

642
00:46:41,784 --> 00:46:49,998
We said that you had Arab pagan worshippers, and you had Arab Muslims and then you had Jews.

643
00:46:50,888 --> 00:46:59,333
And in this multi faith and multi ethnic society, there were some disputes, conflicts going on.

644
00:46:59,849 --> 00:47:06,887
And we mentioned the example of, when Rasool Allah ﷺ went to give Naseeha(نصيحه) in this gathering of a men in Madina

645
00:47:07,433 --> 00:47:11,238
and Abdullah Bin Ubaye(عبدالله بن ابيئ) complaint and said don't come and bother us with your stories,

646
00:47:11,900 --> 00:47:13,470
war was almost going to break out.

647
00:47:14,120 --> 00:47:20,262
So, Rasool Allah ﷺ was now building a nation an Ummah(امة) based on Eeman(إيمان).

648
00:47:20,620 --> 00:47:27,457
Therefore the former relationships need to be dissolved.

649
00:47:28,302 --> 00:47:33,206
So, the Ayaat(آيات) of Qur'an were being revealed to break down the former alliances.

650
00:47:34,055 --> 00:47:35,512
So, Allahعَزّوجَلّ says;

651
00:47:36,340 --> 00:47:45,390
يَا أَيُّهَا الَّذِينَ آمَنُوا لَا تَتَّخِذُوا آبَاءَكُمْ وَإِخْوَانَكُمْ أَوْلِيَاءَ إِنِ اسْتَحَبُّوا الْكُفْرَ عَلَى الْإِيمَانِ ۚ

652
00:47:45,867 --> 00:47:49,664
وَمَنْ يَتَوَلَّهُمْ مِنْكُمْ فَأُولَٰئِكَ هُمُ الظَّالِمُونَ۝

653
00:47:50,260 --> 00:47:51,635
O you, who have believed,

654
00:47:52,640 --> 00:48:00,716
Do not take your father's or your brothers as allies, if they have preferred disbelief over belief.

655
00:48:01,290 --> 00:48:05,975
And whoever does so among you, then it is those who are the wrongdoers.

656
00:48:06,575 --> 00:48:10,536
So, Allahعَزّوجَلّ is now telling the Muslims that you need to terminate

657
00:48:11,063 --> 00:48:15,886
the relationships of loyalty that you have with your tribes, if they're not Muslim.

658
00:48:17,310 --> 00:48:18,587
And Allahعَزّوجَلّ says;

659
00:48:19,004 --> 00:48:32,503
يَا أَيُّهَا الَّذِينَ آمَنُوا لَا تَتَّخِذُوا عَدُوِّي وَعَدُوَّكُمْ أَوْلِيَاءَ تُلْقُونَ إِلَيْهِمْ بِالْمَوَدَّةِ وَقَدْ

660
00:48:32,892 --> 00:48:38,679
وَقَدْ كَفَرُوا بِمَا جَاءَكُمْ مِنَ الْحَقِّ

661
00:48:39,163 --> 00:48:50,100
يُخْرِجُونَ الرَّسُولَ وَإِيَّاكُمْ ۙ أَنْ تُؤْمِنُوا بِاللَّهِ رَبِّكُمْ إِنْ كُنْتُمْ خَرَجْتُمْ جِهَادًا

662
00:48:50,854 --> 00:48:59,403
إنْ كُنْتُمْ خَرَجْتُمْ جِهَادًا فِي سَبِيلِي وَابْتِغَاءَ مَرْضَاتِي ۚ

663
00:48:59,956 --> 00:49:09,822
تُسِرُّونَ إِلَيْهِمْ بِالْمَوَدَّةِ وَأَنَا أَعْلَمُ بِمَا أَخْفَيْتُمْ وَمَا أَعْلَنْتُمْ ۚ

664
00:49:10,211 --> 00:49:17,530
وَمَنْ يَفْعَلْهُ مِنْكُمْ فَقَدْ ضَلَّ سَوَاءَ السَّبِيلِ۝

665
00:49:18,534 --> 00:49:30,369
إِنْ يَثْقَفُوكُمْ يَكُونُوا لَكُمْ أَعْدَاءً وَيَبْسُطُوا إِلَيْكُمْ أَيْدِيَهُمْ وَأَلْسِنَتَهُمْ

666
00:49:30,814 --> 00:49:39,055
وَيَبْسُطُوا إِلَيْكُمْ أَيْدِيَهُمْ وَأَلْسِنَتَهُمْ بِالسُّوءِ وَوَدُّوا

667
00:49:39,357 --> 00:49:42,341
وَوَدُّوا لَوْ تَكْفُرُونَ۝

668
00:49:42,733 --> 00:49:49,267
لَنْ تَنْفَعَكُمْ أَرْحَامُكُمْ وَلَا أَوْلَادُكُمْ ۚ

669
00:49:49,815 --> 00:49:57,597
يَوْمَ الْقِيَامَةِ يَفْصِلُ بَيْنَكُمْ ۚ وَاللَّهُ بِمَا تَعْمَلُونَ بَصِيرٌ۝

670
00:49:58,161 --> 00:49:59,623
O, you who have believed,

671
00:49:59,851 --> 00:50:03,262
do not take My enemies and your enemies as allies,

672
00:50:03,551 --> 00:50:09,006
extending to them affection, while they have disbelieved in what came to you of the truth,

673
00:50:09,422 --> 00:50:13,648
having driven out the prophet and yourselves because you believe in Allah, your Lord.

674
00:50:14,505 --> 00:50:19,480
If you have come out for Jihad(جهاد) in My cause, and seeking means to My approval.

675
00:50:19,681 --> 00:50:23,663
Take them not as friends, you confide to them affection.

676
00:50:24,080 --> 00:50:28,430
But I am most knowing of what you have concealed, and what you have declared.

677
00:50:28,981 --> 00:50:34,035
And whoever does it, among you has certainly strayed from the soundness of the way.

678
00:50:34,829 --> 00:50:36,900
If they gained dominance over you,

679
00:50:37,209 --> 00:50:43,191
they would beat you as enemies and extend against you their hands and their tongues with evil.

680
00:50:43,681 --> 00:50:45,826
And they wish you would disbelieve,

681
00:50:46,501 --> 00:50:50,871
never will your relatives or your children benefit you the Day of Resurrection,

682
00:50:51,014 --> 00:50:55,569
 He will judge between you, and Allah of what you do, is seeing.

683
00:50:56,131 --> 00:50:57,837
So, now you have new rules,

684
00:50:58,584 --> 00:51:04,364
that these former alliances, the loyalty that you used to give to the tribe needs to end.

685
00:51:05,809 --> 00:51:10,659
Now, this is talking about the relationship between the Muslim and Non Muslim in general.

686
00:51:10,904 --> 00:51:12,931
But then there are some specific Ayaat(آيات)

687
00:51:13,011 --> 00:51:17,939
that came to talk about the relationship of the Muslim with the People of the Book, specifically.

688
00:51:19,059 --> 00:51:21,330
The people of the box of Christians and the Jews. Why?

689
00:51:21,823 --> 00:51:24,267
Because in Madina, now we have people of the book.

690
00:51:25,152 --> 00:51:29,298
And the Arabs had, this ongoing relationship with Al-Yahood(أليهود)

691
00:51:29,671 --> 00:51:34,227
whether it is a neighborly relationship, or it is an economical relationship

692
00:51:34,282 --> 00:51:38,614
because of all the economical interests that existed between the two sides,

693
00:51:38,812 --> 00:51:43,314
or whether it was pacts of protection, political relationship.

694
00:51:44,685 --> 00:51:48,337
So, Allahعَزّوجَلّ was revealing Ayaat(آيات) to deal with that issue.

695
00:51:48,996 --> 00:51:50,369
Allahعَزّوجَلّ says;

696
00:51:50,762 --> 00:52:03,226
يَا أَيُّهَا الَّذِينَ آمَنُوا لَا تَتَّخِذُوا الْيَهُودَ وَالنَّصَارَىٰ أَوْلِيَاءَ ۘ

697
00:52:03,762 --> 00:52:07,778
بَعْضُهُمْ أَوْلِيَاءُ بَعْضٍ ۚ

698
00:52:08,119 --> 00:52:13,919
وَمَنْ يَتَوَلَّهُمْ مِنْكُمْ فَإِنَّهُ مِنْهُمْ ۗ

699
00:52:14,142 --> 00:52:19,451
إِنَّ اللَّهَ لَا يَهْدِي الْقَوْمَ الظَّالِمِينَ۝

700
00:52:20,296 --> 00:52:27,310
O you have believed, do not take the Jews and Christians as allies, they are allies of one another.

701
00:52:27,886 --> 00:52:32,972
And whoever is an ally to them among you, then indeed, he is one of them.

702
00:52:33,667 --> 00:52:37,984
Therefore, the meaning of this part; He is one of them! is that a Muslim has became a non Muslim,

703
00:52:38,008 --> 00:52:42,325
a Muslim has disbelieved if he takes the people of the book as allies,

704
00:52:42,667 --> 00:52:45,662
Indeed Allah guides, not the wrongdoing people.

705
00:52:46,115 --> 00:52:47,284
And Allahعَزّوجَلّ says;

706
00:52:47,460 --> 00:52:58,793
يَا أَيُّهَا الَّذِينَ آمَنُوا إِنْ تُطِيعُوا فَرِيقًا مِنَ الَّذِينَ أُوتُوا الْكِتَابَ

707
00:52:59,230 --> 00:53:09,825
إِنْ تُطِيعُوا فَرِيقًا مِنَ الَّذِينَ أُوتُوا الْكِتَابَ يَرُدُّوكُمْ بَعْدَ إِيمَانِكُمْ كَافِرِينَ۝

708
00:53:10,202 --> 00:53:18,661
وَكَيْفَ تَكْفُرُونَ وَأَنْتُمْ تُتْلَىٰ عَلَيْكُمْ آيَاتُ اللَّهِ وَفِيكُمْ رَسُولُهُ ۗ

709
00:53:18,962 --> 00:53:27,134
وَمَنْ يَعْتَصِمْ بِاللَّهِ فَقَدْ هُدِيَ إِلَىٰ صِرَاطٍ مُسْتَقِيمٍ۝

710
00:53:27,392 --> 00:53:28,761
"O, you have believed

711
00:53:29,237 --> 00:53:32,674
if you obey a party of those, who are given the Scripture,

712
00:53:32,857 --> 00:53:37,195
 they will turn you back after your belief to being unbelievers.

713
00:53:38,010 --> 00:53:44,261
And how could you disbelieve, while to you are being recited the verses of Allah

714
00:53:44,483 --> 00:53:46,316
and among you is His Messenger

715
00:53:46,641 --> 00:53:50,549
and whoever holds firmly to Allah has been guided to a straight path.

716
00:53:51,066 --> 00:53:52,472
So, Allah is telling the Muslims;

717
00:53:52,654 --> 00:53:58,162
If you follow the ways of the People of the Book, who are living among you, in Madina, you're going to become disbelievers.

718
00:53:58,922 --> 00:54:00,454
And Allahعَزّوجَلّ says;

719
00:54:01,343 --> 00:54:03,374
And Allah is teaching us, this rule.

720
00:54:03,626 --> 00:54:08,227
This is not talking about an exception, this is not talking about a particular period of history.

721
00:54:08,595 --> 00:54:12,307
Allah is telling us about something that will remain constant until the day of Judgment.

722
00:54:13,491 --> 00:54:18,081
And never will the Jews and the Christians approve of you, until you follow their religion.

723
00:54:19,253 --> 00:54:22,674
Say indeed the guidance of Allah is the only guidance,

724
00:54:22,928 --> 00:54:27,530
if you were to follow their desires, after what has come to you of knowledge,

725
00:54:27,823 --> 00:54:31,363
you would have against Allah, no protector.

726
00:54:33,019 --> 00:54:37,789
So now, all of these relationships of loyalty are negated.

727
00:54:39,326 --> 00:54:43,697
So, you have cut all of these relationships.

728
00:54:44,033 --> 00:54:44,707
Now what.?

729
00:54:45,126 --> 00:54:45,907
You know, just like with

730
00:54:45,947 --> 00:54:46,954
لا اله الا الله

731
00:54:47,295 --> 00:54:49,940
It starts with negating, and then it affirms

732
00:54:50,511 --> 00:54:51,416
لا اله

733
00:54:51,638 --> 00:54:52,527
 there is no god,

734
00:54:52,590 --> 00:54:56,360
so it negates divinity from any deity.

735
00:54:56,932 --> 00:55:00,630
There's no one worthy of worship, that's how it starts,

736
00:55:00,986 --> 00:55:05,940
and then it affirms after it negates the divinity of any deity.

737
00:55:06,265 --> 00:55:07,286
After that it affirms

738
00:55:07,341 --> 00:55:08,341
اِلَّا الله

739
00:55:08,794 --> 00:55:09,895
لا اله الا الله

740
00:55:09,967 --> 00:55:12,246
there is no one worthy of worship except Allah.

741
00:55:12,587 --> 00:55:16,588
Same thing here, this concept in Islam is called Al-Wala Wal Bara'a(ألولآء ولبرآء)

742
00:55:16,739 --> 00:55:19,025
which is important article of Aqeedah(عقيده).

743
00:55:19,301 --> 00:55:21,665
After it negates the relationship, we showed that

744
00:55:21,942 --> 00:55:26,252
Allah is saying that, you shouldn't take your fathers and your brothers, Auleaa(أوليآء) except Allah,

745
00:55:26,339 --> 00:55:28,547
 you shouldn't take the People of the Book Auleaa(أوليآء) except Allah.

746
00:55:28,686 --> 00:55:30,600
So, it negates all of these relationships.

747
00:55:30,758 --> 00:55:34,703
And then it affirms, who our loyalty should be given to.?

748
00:55:34,877 --> 00:55:36,193
Allahعَزّوجَلّ says;

749
00:55:36,725 --> 00:55:46,613
إِنَّمَا وَلِيُّكُمُ اللَّهُ وَرَسُولُهُ وَالَّذِينَ آمَنُوا الَّذِينَ يُقِيمُونَ الصَّلَاةَ

750
00:55:47,248 --> 00:55:54,396
الَّذِينَ يُقِيمُونَ الصَّلَاةَ وَيُؤْتُونَ الزَّكَاةَ وَهُمْ رَاكِعُونَ۝

751
00:55:54,713 --> 00:56:00,912
وَمَنْ يَتَوَلَّ اللَّهَ وَرَسُولَهُ وَالَّذِينَ آمَنُوا

752
00:56:01,221 --> 00:56:06,755
فَإِنَّ حِزْبَ اللَّهِ هُمُ الْغَالِبُونَ۝

753
00:56:07,206 --> 00:56:13,924
Your ally is none, but Allah and His Messenger and those who have believed.

754
00:56:14,420 --> 00:56:17,118
These are the ones, you should give your loyalty to.

755
00:56:17,816 --> 00:56:21,448
Your ally is none but Allah and His Messenger,

756
00:56:21,725 --> 00:56:29,414
and those who have believed, those who establish prayer and give Zakah(زكواة) and they bow, meaning they pray.

757
00:56:29,870 --> 00:56:35,187
And whoever is an ally of Allah and His Messenger, and those who have believed

758
00:56:35,306 --> 00:56:39,284
 indeed the party of Allah, they will be the predominant.

759
00:56:39,495 --> 00:56:44,832
So now, a new community is being established, a community based on faith.

760
00:56:45,784 --> 00:56:47,066
Allahعَزّوجَلّ says;

761
00:56:47,367 --> 00:56:51,277
مُحَمَّدٌ رَسُولُ اللَّهِ ۚ

762
00:56:51,467 --> 00:56:59,651
وَالَّذِينَ مَعَهُ أَشِدَّاءُ عَلَى الْكُفَّارِ رُحَمَاءُ بَيْنَهُمْ ۖ

763
00:57:00,055 --> 00:57:08,529
تَرَاهُمْ رُكَّعًا سُجَّدًا يَبْتَغُونَ فَضْلًا مِنَ اللَّهِ وَرِضْوَانًا ۖ

764
00:57:08,886 --> 00:57:14,504
سِيمَاهُمْ فِي وُجُوهِهِمْ مِنْ أَثَرِ السُّجُودِ ۚ

765
00:57:14,786 --> 00:57:18,655
ذَٰلِكَ مَثَلُهُمْ فِي التَّوْرَاةِ ۚ

766
00:57:18,893 --> 00:57:26,893
وَمَثَلُهُمْ فِي الْإِنْجِيلِ كَزَرْعٍ أَخْرَجَ شَطْأَهُ فَآزَرَهُ فَاسْتَغْلَظَ

767
00:57:27,214 --> 00:57:37,156
فَآزَرَهُ فَاسْتَغْلَظَ فَاسْتَوَىٰ عَلَىٰ سُوقِهِ يُعْجِبُ الزُّرَّاعَ لِيَغِيظَ بِهِمُ الْكُفَّارَ ۗ

768
00:57:37,495 --> 00:57:47,910
وَعَدَ اللَّهُ الَّذِينَ آمَنُوا وَعَمِلُوا الصَّالِحَاتِ مِنْهُمْ مَغْفِرَةً وَأَجْرًا عَظِيمًا۝

769
00:57:49,896 --> 00:57:51,817
"Muhammad(محمد) is the Messenger of Allah,

770
00:57:52,293 --> 00:57:55,507
and those with him are forceful against the disbelievers,

771
00:57:55,716 --> 00:57:57,610
merciful among themselves.

772
00:57:58,111 --> 00:58:00,459
You see them bowing and prostrating

773
00:58:00,896 --> 00:58:03,441
seeking bounty from Allah and His pleasure.

774
00:58:03,838 --> 00:58:07,428
Their mark is on their faces from the trace of prostrations.

775
00:58:07,737 --> 00:58:10,042
That is the description in the Torah(توراة).

776
00:58:10,356 --> 00:58:15,969
And their description in the Gospel, is as a plant which produces its offshoots

777
00:58:16,300 --> 00:58:22,654
and strengthens them, so they grow firm and stand upon their stocks delighting the source,

778
00:58:23,158 --> 00:58:26,940
so that He, Allah May enrage by them, the disbelievers

779
00:58:27,884 --> 00:58:34,733
Allah has promised those who believe and do righteous deeds among them, forgiveness and a great reward.

780
00:58:36,420 --> 00:58:42,305
We talk about some of the virtues of Al-Ansaar(أنْصَار), the ones who sacrificed for Rasool Allah ﷺ.

781
00:58:44,653 --> 00:58:47,329
Rasool Allah ﷺ says in Bukhari(بخاري);

782
00:58:47,686 --> 00:58:52,247
 لَا يُحٍبُّهُمْ اِلَّا مُؤمِنْ، وَلَا يَبْغَضُهُمْ اِلَّا مُنَافِقْ،

783
00:58:52,700 --> 00:58:57,105
فَمَنْ اَحَبَّهُمْ اَحَبَّهُ الله ،وَمَنْ اَبْغَضَهُمْ اَبْغَضَهُ الله

784
00:58:58,095 --> 00:59:04,177
Only a believer would love them, and only a Munafiq(منافق), a hypocrite would hate them.

785
00:59:04,983 --> 00:59:12,201
And whoever loves them, Allah will love him and whoever hates them, Allah will hate him or Allah will dislike him.

786
00:59:13,407 --> 00:59:14,737
 Rasool Allah ﷺ says;

787
00:59:14,880 --> 00:59:20,806
لَوْ اَنَّ الْاَنْصَارَ سَلَكُوْ وَادِيًّ اَوْ شِعْبًا لَسَلَكْتُ وَادِيًّ الْاَنْصَارْ

788
00:59:21,282 --> 00:59:23,957
وَلَوْ لَلْهِجْرَهْ لَكُنْتُمْ رِئِنْ مِّنَ الْاَنْصَارْ

789
00:59:24,356 --> 00:59:25,461
This is in Bukhari(ألبخاري).

790
00:59:26,501 --> 00:59:31,430
If the Ansaar(أنْصَار) take one path, and the rest of the people would take another path

791
00:59:31,612 --> 00:59:33,516
I would follow the path of Al-Ansaar(الأنْصَار).

792
00:59:33,833 --> 00:59:38,794
And if it wasn't that I have made Hijrah(هجرة), I would consider myself a member of Al-Ansaar(الأنْصَار).

793
00:59:40,321 --> 00:59:41,678
Rasool Allah ﷺ says;

794
00:59:41,758 --> 00:59:47,602
اَللَّهُمَّ اغْفِرْ لِلْأَنْصَارِ، وَلِأَبْنَاءِ الأَنْصَارِ، وَلِأَبْنَاءِ أَبْنَاءِ الأَنْصَار، وَلِنِسَاءِ الاَنْصَارْ

795
00:59:48,118 --> 00:59:53,214
Rasool Allah ﷺ says in Bukhari(بخاريْ); O Allah forgive the Ansaar(أنْصَار), and the children of Al-Ansaar(ألأنصار)

796
00:59:53,397 --> 00:59:57,372
and the children of the children of Al-Ansaar(الأنْصَار), and the women of Al-Ansaar(ألأنصار).

797
00:59:58,165 --> 00:59:59,665
And Rasool Allah ﷺ says;

798
01:00:00,237 --> 01:00:09,878
إنَّ الأنْصارَ كَرِشِي وعَيْبَتِي، وإنَّ النَّاسَ سَيَكْثُرُونَ ويَقِلُّونَ، فاقْبَلُوا مِن مُحْسِنِهِمْ واعْفُوا عن سيئِهِمْ

799
01:00:10,753 --> 01:00:15,873
He says that people are going to increase and the Ansaar(أنْصَار) are going to decrease

800
01:00:16,167 --> 01:00:17,976
because now we have a lot of people becoming Muslim.

801
01:00:18,205 --> 01:00:20,828
So, the ratio of Al-Ansaar(ألأنصار) to the rest is going to become few.

802
01:00:21,265 --> 01:00:30,423
So, Rasool Allah ﷺ says; Accept from the one of them who does good and overlook their mistakes, of the ones who commit them.

803
01:00:31,487 --> 01:00:39,182
وَالَّذِيْ نَفْسٌ مُحَمَّدٍ بِيَدِهْ اِنِّيْ لَاُحِبُّكُمْ، إن الأنصارَ قد قضَوا ما عليهم وبقيَ الذي عليكُم

804
01:00:39,638 --> 01:00:43,018
In the name of Allah, I love you, I love Al-Ansaar(الأنْصَار).

805
01:00:43,217 --> 01:00:46,122
And then he said, Al-Ansaar(ألأنصار) have done their part.

806
01:00:46,320 --> 01:00:47,296
Now it's your turn.

807
01:00:47,825 --> 01:00:51,525
He's talking to the rest of the people and telling them, Al-Ansaar(ألأنصار) have done, what they need to do.

808
01:00:51,850 --> 01:00:55,550
It's now your turn to do that to fulfill your duties towards this religion.

809
01:00:56,188 --> 01:01:03,563
So, this is the part regarding the second important project of Rasool Allah ﷺ, in Madina,

810
01:01:03,746 --> 01:01:07,238
and that is establishing a community based on brotherhood,

811
01:01:07,618 --> 01:01:09,887
so I think it's clear from these Ayaat(آيات).

812
01:01:10,335 --> 01:01:14,787
And what we mentioned, the importance of developing brotherhood among the Ummah(امة).

813
01:01:15,478 --> 01:01:19,570
Keep in mind that Shaitan(شيطان) is always trying to disunite us.

814
01:01:20,734 --> 01:01:22,284
So, we have to fight this Waswasa(وسوسه),

815
01:01:23,018 --> 01:01:25,741
and we have to be aware that the Waswasa(وسوسه) is there.

816
01:01:26,207 --> 01:01:31,793
We have to understand that there's someone plotting against us, being brothers.

817
01:01:32,515 --> 01:01:39,317
In order to fight that enemy, Shaitan(شيطان), who's always trying to cause disunity among us.

818
01:01:39,428 --> 01:01:45,632
I mean, one single word, Shaitan(شيطان) can use it to cause a dispute between a Muslim and his brother.

819
01:01:45,952 --> 01:01:47,444
And that's why Allahعَزّوجَلّ says;

820
01:01:47,638 --> 01:01:55,683
وَقُلْ لِعِبَادِي يَقُولُوا الَّتِي هِيَ أَحْسَنُ ۚ إِنَّ الشَّيْطَانَ يَنْزَغُ بَيْنَهُمْ ۚ إِنَّ الشَّيْطَانَ كَانَ لِلْإِنْسَانِ عَدُوًّا مُبِينًا۝

821
01:01:56,319 --> 01:01:59,934
Allahعَزّوجَلّ is saying to Muhammadﷺ, tell my servants to speak good,

822
01:02:00,964 --> 01:02:04,626
because Shaitan(شيطان) is there to cause disunity among them.

823
01:02:05,015 --> 01:02:08,150
And Shaitan(شيطان) is indeed your enemy.

824
01:02:08,513 --> 01:02:14,653
So, Allah is saying that he could take one of those words that you said and cause your brother to misinterpret it

825
01:02:15,424 --> 01:02:16,959
and then causea problem.

826
01:02:17,285 --> 01:02:19,352
So Be careful, of what you say.

827
01:02:19,958 --> 01:02:27,996
The third project which Rasool Allah ﷺ, started when he arrived to Madina was

828
01:02:28,076 --> 01:02:32,544
what is called Al-Waseeqah(اَلْوَثِيْقَة) or the covenant, the document.

829
01:02:33,148 --> 01:02:41,646
This was a document that was written to govern the relationship between the different communities in Madina.

830
01:02:42,340 --> 01:02:46,336
I will read to the terms of this agreement.

831
01:02:47,328 --> 01:02:49,968
It is narrated by Ibn Is'haqq(اِبْنِ اِسْحَاقْ);

832
01:02:50,808 --> 01:02:58,911
The Messenger of Allah wrote a contract between the immigrants and the helpers, in which he expressed conciliation.

833
01:02:58,951 --> 01:03:00,483
 These are the words of Ibn Is'haqq(اِبْنِ اِسْحَاقْ),

834
01:03:00,979 --> 01:03:03,880
I'll start with the terms of the agreement itself.

835
01:03:04,427 --> 01:03:09,598
It says, "In the Name of Allah, the Merciful, the Beneficent.

836
01:03:09,998 --> 01:03:13,508
This is a document from Muhammad(محمد), The unlettered Prophet,

837
01:03:14,055 --> 01:03:20,710
between the believers and Muslims of Quraish(قُرَيْشْ) and Yasrib(يثرب), and their followers, allies and supporters

838
01:03:21,225 --> 01:03:24,829
establishing that they are one nation apart from all others.

839
01:03:25,798 --> 01:03:29,544
The immigrants from Quraish(قُرَيْشْ) will maintain their current practice

840
01:03:29,790 --> 01:03:33,044
and will honor Blood Money contracts between themselves

841
01:03:33,452 --> 01:03:36,630
 and will treat their weaker members with kindness and justice.

842
01:03:37,152 --> 01:03:43,484
The Bannu Auf(بنو عوف) shall maintain their current practice, and honor their former Blood Money contracts,

843
01:03:43,938 --> 01:03:49,745
each party treating their weaker members with kindness and justice among all believers.

844
01:03:50,538 --> 01:03:55,381
He then made reference to each clan of the helpers, and to the families of each home,

845
01:03:55,599 --> 01:04:00,555
mentioning the Bannu Sa'adah(بنو سعاد), the Bannu Jusham(بنو جشم), the Bannu Najjar(بنو نجار), the Bannu Amr Bin Auf( بنو أمر بن عوف) and Bannu Nabit(بنو نابت).

846
01:04:01,090 --> 01:04:07,092
He went on to say, the believers shall not leave anyone among them burdened by debts

847
01:04:07,191 --> 01:04:13,781
without giving to him in kindness, and in paying for him, any ransom money or blood money he owes.

848
01:04:14,793 --> 01:04:19,414
A believer will not ally with any freedman of a second believer against that man.

849
01:04:20,148 --> 01:04:29,840
Pious believers act against any of their own who practice evil or seek to bring harm, sin, aggression, or corruption among believers.

850
01:04:30,832 --> 01:04:36,579
Believers will unite against anyone doing this, even if he be one of their own sons.

851
01:04:37,352 --> 01:04:41,013
No believers shall kill any believer for any non believer,

852
01:04:41,430 --> 01:04:45,481
nor shall he help any non believer against a believer.

853
01:04:46,005 --> 01:04:51,445
So, you can notice here that this concept of community based on faith, Is there.

854
01:04:52,068 --> 01:04:59,496
No believers shall kill any believer for any non believer, nor shall he help any non believer against a believer.

855
01:05:00,329 --> 01:05:06,353
Allah's protection is all one, the least of them can offer protection to others.

856
01:05:06,983 --> 01:05:10,861
Believers are allies to one another, excluding others,

857
01:05:11,003 --> 01:05:15,068
meaning we are a nation apart from anyone, everyone else.

858
01:05:16,106 --> 01:05:20,898
Whatever Jews follow us, shall receive help and equality.

859
01:05:21,632 --> 01:05:27,131
They shall not be maltreated, nor will help be afforded others against them.

860
01:05:27,443 --> 01:05:37,143
No peace shall be accepted for anyone believer to the exclusion of others, when the battle is for Allah's cause.

861
01:05:37,912 --> 01:05:40,733
Among them equality and justice must prevail.

862
01:05:41,432 --> 01:05:46,941
In every expedition we engage in, riders shall take turns on their mounts.

863
01:05:47,535 --> 01:05:51,486
Believers shall avenge one another for bloodshed in Allah's cause.

864
01:05:51,871 --> 01:05:56,170
Believers who are pious are well guided on the straightest of paths.

865
01:05:57,319 --> 01:06:03,479
No Polytheist shall be allowed to offer protection for the property or persons of Quraish(قُرَيْشْ),

866
01:06:03,882 --> 01:06:06,448
nor try to interfere with any believer.

867
01:06:07,132 --> 01:06:12,255
Anyone who has clearly aggressed against and caused the death of any believer

868
01:06:12,430 --> 01:06:18,194
shall be subject to retaliation for him, unless the dead man's executor can be satisfied.

869
01:06:19,312 --> 01:06:26,360
Believers as a whole shall take action against him, and no excuse for they're not doing so will be acceptable.

870
01:06:27,388 --> 01:06:32,029
It shall not be permissible for any believer who has accepted what is in this document,

871
01:06:32,360 --> 01:06:38,167
and who believes in Allah, in Judgment Day to give help or shelter to any wrongdoer.

872
01:06:39,048 --> 01:06:44,814
Any believer who does this shall be the object of Allah's, curses and anger on Judgment Day

873
01:06:45,369 --> 01:06:50,833
and neither compensation, nor excuse will be acceptable from him.

874
01:06:51,780 --> 01:07:00,577
Any matter in which you disagree, must be referred to Allah Almighty and glorious is He and to Muhammadﷺ.

875
01:07:01,748 --> 01:07:07,815
The Jews shall pay expenses along with the Muslims, so long as they are allied in warfare.

876
01:07:08,257 --> 01:07:15,270
The Jews of Banni Auf(بني عوف) are one nation with the believers, the Jews shall have their religion, the Muslims their own.

877
01:07:15,726 --> 01:07:22,724
This applies to their freedmen and to themselves, except for those who commit sins and are unjust.

878
01:07:23,328 --> 01:07:26,714
Such persons only harm themselves and their families.

879
01:07:27,510 --> 01:07:31,410
What applies to Banni Auf(بني عوف) shall also apply to the Jews of Bannu Najjar(بنو نجار),

880
01:07:31,759 --> 01:07:36,013
Bannu Al-Hariss(بنو الحارث), Bannu Sa'adah(بنو سعاده), Bannu Jusham(بنو جشم), Bannu Al-Aos(بنو الاوس),

881
01:07:36,255 --> 01:07:40,559
 Bannu Al-Sa'alabah(بنو ثعلبه) and Jufna(جفنه) and Bannu Shutaibah(شطيبه).

882
01:07:41,160 --> 01:07:44,876
The close associates of the Jews shall be viewed as themselves.

883
01:07:45,412 --> 01:07:48,851
None of them shall go to war without Muhammad's permission.

884
01:07:49,230 --> 01:07:53,733
However he is not there by constraints from taking revenge for injury.

885
01:07:54,730 --> 01:08:04,229
Whoever attacks another may do so, to protect himself and his family, but act not unjustly for Allah condemns such acts.

886
01:08:04,600 --> 01:08:08,237
The Jews shall bear their own expenses, the Muslims their's,

887
01:08:08,566 --> 01:08:13,757
each must help one another against any, who fight those who adopt this document.

888
01:08:14,361 --> 01:08:19,729
They must give one another advice and consultation and do good and avoid evil.

889
01:08:20,721 --> 01:08:24,670
A man is not held blameworthy on behalf of his ally.

890
01:08:25,099 --> 01:08:27,246
Help must be given to those wronged.

891
01:08:27,492 --> 01:08:29,809
The center of Yasrib(يثرب) shall be a sanctuary.

892
01:08:29,986 --> 01:08:31,928
For those who agree to this document.

893
01:08:32,293 --> 01:08:34,897
One's neighbor shall be treated as one self,

894
01:08:35,290 --> 01:08:37,440
without being harmed or sinned against.

895
01:08:38,055 --> 01:08:43,133
No property shall be encroached upon without the permission of its owner.

896
01:08:43,556 --> 01:08:50,227
In the case of any dispute, or incident, occurring between those agreeing to this document

897
01:08:50,251 --> 01:08:53,251
and involving consequences likely to be harmful,

898
01:08:53,569 --> 01:08:57,799
the matter must be referred to Allah and to Muhammad(محمد), the Messenger of Allah.

899
01:08:58,119 --> 01:09:02,440
Allah acknowledges what is very good and very pious in this document,

900
01:09:02,737 --> 01:09:06,217
Quraish(قُرَيْشْ) and those who helped them shall receive no protection.

901
01:09:06,664 --> 01:09:11,687
Those accepting this document must help one another against anyone attacking Yasrib(يثرب).

902
01:09:12,282 --> 01:09:18,072
If they are called upon to make peace, and do so and keep to it, they will be making peace.

903
01:09:18,431 --> 01:09:25,532
If they make similar demand, then it is up to the Muslims to agree except, if the warfare is over the faith.

904
01:09:25,861 --> 01:09:32,352
Each participant shall receive whatever portion is due to him, from his own sides winnings.

905
01:09:32,851 --> 01:09:36,756
This document will not provide protection for anyone sinful or unjust.

906
01:09:37,400 --> 01:09:39,339
Whoever goes to war will be safe

907
01:09:39,561 --> 01:09:41,315
or whoever leaves will be safe.

908
01:09:41,593 --> 01:09:43,839
Whoever stays in the town will be safe,

909
01:09:44,091 --> 01:09:47,203
except for those who have sinned or been unjust.

910
01:09:47,577 --> 01:09:51,267
Allah provides protection for those, who are good and pious."

911
01:09:51,581 --> 01:09:58,373
So, this was the document that Rasool Allah ﷺ wrote to govern the rules, or to govern the communities in Madina.

912
01:09:58,564 --> 01:10:02,731
 In sha Allah Ta'ala(اِن شَاالله تعالى) , we'll make some brief comments on this document tomorrow.

913
01:10:03,021 --> 01:10:07,857
رَبَّنَا آتِنَا فِي الدُّنْيَا حَسَنَةً وَفِي الْآخِرَةِ حَسَنَةً وَقِنَا عَذَابَ النَّارِ َ

914
01:10:08,278 --> 01:10:13,125
وَصَلَّى الله عَلى سَيَّدِنَا محمد وَعَلى اَلِهِ وَ صَحْبِهِ وَسَلِّمْ تَسْلِيْمًا كَثِيْرًاَ

915
01:10:13,279 --> 01:10:15,910
وَ السلام عليكم ورحمة الله وبركاته

